      <Placemark>
        <name>Aqua Marcia (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GzV0FSRvi-dysuPMRE_H8Nywst-ISQXgg1-6YVCdl57Z9y-cGErIoWNQ0-QQqU1i92boa8HXtqjcvYilP-zjBJ_os6PQ4zWpCEy-QscsNxESesp7pd8pDMcCaznUBoU9sdEa7FCIDbt5l_cBfOC3lo3KUV5c2-Hqlq6hxi3gCmffeff2WVOnYsjgrGDU6bStiBq_M_wweq2lw?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Marcian Aqueduct, Rome.<br><br>The Aqua Marcia was constructed from 144 to 140 BC by the praetor Quintus Marcius Rex (an ancestor of Julius Caesar), for whom it is named.<br><br>The aqueduct was largely paid for by spoils from the recent Roman conquests of Corinth in 146 BC and the destruction of Carthage at the end of the Third Punic War, in the same year.<br><br>The aqueduct followed the via Tiburtina into Rome, and entered the city in its eastern boundary at the Porta Tiburtina of the Aurelian Wall. It was well known for its cold and pure waters.<br><br>The aqueduct was repaired by Marcus Agrippa in 33 BC, and then later again by Augustus, according to the inscription in the arch that was later made into the Porta Tiburtina. Augustus also augmented the supply by linking it to an additional source, the Aqua Augusta, doubling the throughput. Much of its supply was siphoned off by private citizens for their own use, making it effectively only a trickle in the city by the time of Nero. The supply was increased again by later emperors. Frontinus measured the flow of the Aqua Marcia at its source around 97 AD as 4690 quinariae, making it the second-greatest source of the city's water.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1703-A52714</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GzV0FSRvi-dysuPMRE_H8Nywst-ISQXgg1-6YVCdl57Z9y-cGErIoWNQ0-QQqU1i92boa8HXtqjcvYilP-zjBJ_os6PQ4zWpCEy-QscsNxESesp7pd8pDMcCaznUBoU9sdEa7FCIDbt5l_cBfOC3lo3KUV5c2-Hqlq6hxi3gCmffeff2WVOnYsjgrGDU6bStiBq_M_wweq2lw?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
