      <Placemark>
        <name>Bibliotheca Graeca et Latina (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gx4Bz54HQCmzK2A8bvg-u69nLY7VLOWDTb-DU8tjDZf3H9t2ZyuV25W_r7-xD79rRa8RObAkydzTv26tezLiBfKRjAecVqZHml0UJv6y9veEHNddoZ61ksM4eIpxWKI1bb8zo4sbGvdsdBzzDBZzGAwyMr_KruEQ_hdCFCM4u6mziECkS-Zy0NtHX3HjBR9Zmd9WnKg34vH3g?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Library of Greek and Latin, Rome.<br><br>This library, located SE of the Palatine Temple of Apollo, had both Greek and Latin collections. It may have been dedicated in 28 BC together with the Temple of Apollo, although it was not mentioned along with the Portico of the Danaids and Temple of Apollo in the second book of Propertius published in or before 24 BC. <br><br>The library was a versatile space, and in addition to storing a dual-language manuscript collection it served as the locale for a number of Senate meetings during Augustus’ reign, especially during his old age.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1526-A52714</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gx4Bz54HQCmzK2A8bvg-u69nLY7VLOWDTb-DU8tjDZf3H9t2ZyuV25W_r7-xD79rRa8RObAkydzTv26tezLiBfKRjAecVqZHml0UJv6y9veEHNddoZ61ksM4eIpxWKI1bb8zo4sbGvdsdBzzDBZzGAwyMr_KruEQ_hdCFCM4u6mziECkS-Zy0NtHX3HjBR9Zmd9WnKg34vH3g?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
