      <Placemark>
        <name>Carcer (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v7pR0IIS4n4IpFizRwU4nhlWAvDJd_t4aU361Mq2ylk7BtoFHGlfok4tov5T3tuyGSgKQDNN-dsE3W50ldvKwD6-ygAzbs35C2lYjeJSytK-cdTRDJGM-95Tv0p5f4uYMs6cfEgl-hD9vlC0kZehahV-oJFwHCdwWAWvEQp0AJBCHE7db2jFObFf-j2S4yiSXeInaSiQIVDEB2QELcldpxreCJa84Fsh-1pZHs-zhsV9D7OM0eC5Q5_6accksCxOI5CsiBi0sFPrsPiZHsgN4Ux5xThUEQeL0hFlbkSOXEKbTW1XwH3G7YdE94rO0QWu-99wZzTW4VMJZHzbVGccPegC2YTv2B6Gd-zJq9pJhCAG2B5lj4iXNcpwZCMtQ2Tecv_QXnJku18nNfRaDqoXlPjbEBjB_tSrOdo59_tfyXetNXwg9Zea5lhBHiI5cPOVZb0453ZwpxJCea4w4AWQ8CnZvyhZTHE3nIdk7XyQDzgoFEBzueSe0QZp5T7sQrQT9A0rs1gR2cjnccneV745r3at-Sztwzc500MEPYqLw6WUjl2f43fFC6GBmLleKm-myiP5TjxrwW5oEnwAq-l0U5av_DvGyvyfUhjdFzEPjK8jRSL0nkNDq6vtih1tSxHP_rMsbUJtQVitu3aQLfAzxFUVKzZoE6VYjj6RbBYfNwNJGep7rmreio2yedwX1TidYi6yzPEIJpl9w" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Prison, Rome.<br><br>This was the only public prison in Rome, used as a place of brief detention and execution, not for long imprisonment. <br><br>Sources use two terms, Carcer and Tullianum, but these are not strictly synonymous. The former refers to the whole; the latter refers to a part located underground. Its location is given as imminens foro, ‘touching the Forum’, close to the Temple of Concordia Augusta, and next to the steps that led up to the Arx. From the literary testimonia, we may identify the Carcer with the building under the Church of S. Giuseppe dei Falegnami. It fits the known location of the Carcer and preserves the architectural division between an upper and a lower level. Underneath is a well-preserved circular chamber (diam. 7 m) for which Coarelli records a date of c. 300 BC. Around 100 BC a flat-arched roof was added and a trapezoidal chamber built above, its outer walls oriented along the axes of the Temple of Concordia Augusta to the S and the Comitium to the E. Both upper and lower levels stood beneath ground level, so the Carcer was defined more by its interior than exterior space. It may also have been part of a larger complex.<br><br><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v7gWU1DkjjaM5h4CaUD_oGu2lQC8fLAEU4qc1bJYQuR-nDaYI65YMwOWLL_f4YuCG5wBYvEkuwQ3Aq1kyGnXQyLIKerwhKBnRIWy4G2WrTEtq9kdzjbDRmsaIK07RkmzqaxpE53qbHxDR7CBEvr9H1HRgTV6WDboLCz5EEWULbnNPwMrFFLkrXXiYYQEIczkMT8jif6MgX6khcr50tNP1h1w3sZeX1Kgt0fQ9qmQ4-jeXuGQnJLPd3I6ULm8Dtjxzyg4P2xjCb9x0d65Q2hv-deqtVjQiBlkPefA3If3AvUEvnkju3e6Q4w2tcyVWhaSIaHx0hXG6aKvsUKuRlMp6SSh8bBCjQBPEaMVVceeNcH4ezJQFtqJiV1MCMUNlfp4juwy3OefMnvrSowPcZAwDpiPEToXwDXVwQalkJe-qoU3Q6xjai8NlljPsSyVsc5_E5ZqhrS9kBn-nFichLRge-VVj_nKR03HYap1Ug1ijy9vBFxlnRiUuSDuknXBR0GtmwgffgikuxpkRHF_yIEpej8klenerBHYNk652Iwt9bIxwUHMQZATOlKlf7KiOu11RM6jUoKvnqq_431hZTyHXXlNHejGJuQ5EMyqgjji_yIqkhnZ-nm4BMXoIwCs0JlFqgRUR3jOwcs42O3SwNcBsPZRr6gB-eOL-Sx8t-6g37phFYcf1_-6EPSNyQMFh04v34C22eEPy1qkA" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
