      <Placemark>
        <name>Columna Phocae (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v6aPz39RPOcF63D39mVR0GQKclxjP14E8H_ssPSCxNebyOdlLA-v4uLBSVYubNe5fAPcVVHbChaJP4m15qJ6IErV3_XNR8kG5m0e9epXZjC3C7cIQWaOSJCXBtfv-PpOl9R5URuK4YbEy9AcPzweU1W5AnzaFr4ABVHlkQqaoK6zwNY_O5vGmv51jBBgxIHQMkZW1-YIWHTR2qNfB7Nw2jxsuv5dkCkFJzdpfO41AXhBBN0gIU_B6Mtn4XRSOPRz5VyxwgUdnBiLfwj4y7tYJF0DKsF0kG9t0kfxvOAqiG3aVTqpLnQfXo5wu7AQUc61x_61NciapUdqZlM3JlzX9OUPV1U1GdGkJLYizdbMkckKYnyufwtdBzdoA3y3FIZp9DVR-tcLxIt3qQtWIy7qFx1u7BRr3MS4sC5HnW1rGuD7nUFDmhyT5vgSf7R0tB81YUkTUqVVuK-HAbhcZztojOlfdDQdW99PqEh7mOjO2jsGUqrjM8pubFbKp6pqbwaK54pExipWezSvFQhOUwmp4Wjy0ImNIjHigyH9n-HYGEgZGlt-qeDsM-A4quluZaZbL5TlCbo67EEt_i7-tSm21TSsqgwq0p7W_oPsQ2o8tl_-6oAFxS8Q9kPsf5QD6aiTJMRVqB_Xew6hSob-Gaql7idG1fBrnsOvzIOlQAjof3ZpDK2bhQCa0_yED8QFkaacFn9YOvZMy4YXA" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Column of Phocas, Rome.<br><br>It is a monumental column in the Roman Forum of Rome. Erected in front of the Rostra and dedicated or rededicated in honour of the Eastern Roman Emperor Phocas on August 1, 608, it was the last addition made to the Forum Romanum. The fluted Corinthian column stands 13.6 m (44 ft) tall on its cubical white marble socle. On stylistic grounds, the column seems to have been made in the 2nd century for an unknown structure, and then recycled for the present monument. Likewise, the socle was recycled from its original use supporting a statue dedicated to Diocletian.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1599-A52714</styleUrl>
