      <Placemark>
        <name>Curia Pompeia (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v4R3XTsyTW4nF7gLS9U32j3gPQmeDLkmRgu7t9e7n0Vy_U2A7mNhRaca8yQb0uo-7iMAWpeKh4Sk9-JdR8rvSSc1irNidhQ3kBdq959LODrZwERP6DT1FkVYIcYoTXTcEe4kvMB6EEHT9CF1lRVGEKSYE4e9BIsS7vYKnTYVZ4QEDD5WFhNFF6KHvEq3s-5ExpHocarWXwQwLHzoD5jWBcUuaUHkUdnpW0dPtPG7YwkzETYkDTlB3eAr0V932vYv2hrc23sJqBaAvecJgcT85U6kCJJWUexS_ksd4XB-I3G6aIpK031BcqrCZfzGxyyOx6iYrflA6wFtLgHpi1YqM0wOSvhCOn6qKbicss77Vfd1MNOHS5SAbx22BOU4vG_4cG1T0hKJu5ez-BjINsZCHaKsa46XPxwrEVeTymuROKaWjyur0IaOUrDymiUF5H7eaBoZ4UYdCI9CVOCG0wcw2NjonelACPC2zfoMX9Fsytg4he4OcaCSoxO5HSvaL6bFHFimM2Nfvjk4TJB7ap0CkLnR3oJJrYe-L_9-DCbQ_k_kG7iV1Q8ccJO2chjW0QYL28104atPuoocSgm0pPYfppCtpjSHHgBLCoTXRAXxBPl3rOV0PiYWmkRvXKcxxn2vvVyL4FHSgKNYJWHiKnxZ0yAdlJzKC0VLJXzyz07JbbTsBh1KJLyGk64GIGR2bZfxuw2R7Cl3Y_YQw" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Senate House, Rome<br><br>The senate-house built by Cn. Pompeius Magnus at the same time as the Theatrum Pompeium in 55 BC stood as an exedra at the E end of the Porticus Pompeia. In 44 BC Julius Caesar was assassinated here, and the Curia Pompeia was burned by mourners at his funeral. In 42 B.C. it was walled up by the triumvirs and left as a memorial to Caesar’s death.<br><br> It has been identified with the tufa remains in opus quadratum (c.20 x 24 m) behind the Temple of Fortuna Huiusce Diei in the “Area Sacra” in Largo Argentina. In the Augustan period, the Curia Pompeia no longer functioned as a senate-house, but the building remained as a charred, walled-up memorial.]]></description>
