      <Placemark>
        <name>Euripus (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v4Q2AsebRVWWkxJgwsdcdZl5Uak1OTbPNq3aSoBxUH7XSRVEl-pP_xDhFFexU7nB5CNBPRsve7hJtnDnkuawG3h0vNuXSMe4pkqQNhfRejp0QIloGpwMNsgCoz4mxb_kSpe2CkrT2bOuU6MmRNo5NhsUy7NsX1uRxXQrxYH9FQfa3zspTTVy7FwEpz_Gku1aoizLfBEhSJjHuNzFo6CI06RByYPT80GbnabbS-sQeuTeTlFnG6zYra6IiKlk-RILEXBNjxKWbtxnnU-ou31l_qew2oyYnIQ1KwfI0emgU-JpF85XSMgDyk_XBb54hWk02jdMWwe6WFkLsL1HTKRVQvH6sRU9hMti20ILcYO-uCXI7_7yY22dIRR9IQKx2P8fE1-Oe4ZS9YABBwCHUxWh6GHhbTh5uqcpEbIgkDZQG6uxgCi1pIDtmxraOPh2unF4YYZSuR5BRmke7S3u-Kv6wg_TlEKiZD61GU8LtkhZ2AbdMwe_JXhIXdE_Pon9r6RyEIzrsHMLHN_Me-c-hW6YXCJ1QcRHyl8tu648Lwgfi5nwURSWwWQw6tyfNQqyioCDUO8tjBAImjsa8ZGnzPBa_7WZdqOcyH54OMDZL0fqd_LpAwG_RY7_6Tr6exZ2v5kfXqh8leYDoGgNdIFE_SJFVZBFMZ11TCkoOCUEDzU4jZ0WIR6Mwj_WzHl2bAm79AOscpQqmCl3R8IEA" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Water Channel, Rome<br><br>An artifical water channel constructed by Agrippa across the W Campus Martius in order to drain the Stagnum Agrippae into the Tiber. <br><br>Fed by the Aqua Virgo with clear running water, the Euripus had a great urbanistic impact and played a vital rôle in Agrippa’s building campaign on the Campus Martius. Part of the Euripus can be seen on the Severan Marble Plan and archaeological evidence allows its course to be plotted with relative accuracy. The Euripus is thought to have run parallel to the Tiber in the NW Campus Martius, and scattered remains of its channel have been recovered there. The channel had a semicircular section (diam. 1.73 m) and was flanked by two parallel walls in opus reticulatum and tufa ashlar masonry; these building techniques, combined with the use of marble and travertine elsewhere in the structure, suggest an early Augustan date for the Euripus. Moreover, the stratigraphic level of these remains, which corresponds approximately to that of the Republican Sepulcrum: A. Hirtius, would not sustain a later attribution.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1703-A52714</styleUrl>
