      <Placemark>
        <name>Pons Agrippa (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v4RSlIwxjRI31dwBCRwhnTd2v-eErfJuqiKZUtnFLWRReYWIAGb5vLaMP-6O7YV--_KgT8z0mnHyCjalEepO9veQFYkpz8MgVFWiQQ-_YmMPhvM49LTtCjPy61192wFRPOQ3fFBQXNK4jJjeIGXXBQeO5B0aHn65pz1u0qLuufNEk0SYLYoQBJXxBunsBbnQ126cwnofZIMPoq8SxYPn-Kl99b16yVn3LS4B2YKqhbmN2VRSJDyFVITi9aQQA9YjFoZxAVrczlhX06_QmPlZbMQeorCqPUHegTkF2UocwxaxuvxP8qKhwxQj2myfUH8du99UrkIMlH0w-gKYVIAHfeU5MOErJl7VNUfHxx79i5g75o6sabzfx-i4GiDi3366o1_z0lpl7f-vjbRu1bx59_ypK5nbY1mthkd3L-SfTUvO_G_HXHpjFCQhHwo9t0BItm5zjQwUOwlt9hEXO5Qz6qPUuZlx5ujLp8X8xA3uGpeN_mBVttjOV0GsVnn8GW-11rdiEp-Ole5PD__vpYEYKLivyHgvPFgAgOuMwJ_N1XCGVbmvlYjYA1VFoL5ggHXbnLBAbvzs9xM4sGf-gEKlYU2lyZ6Khib5Xwh567oEwHlpddc71IpEvW0Rl3tH7uIj9gHBqCz5mQ5R3bPJcA82GUkkrJMbf6tkzLRMBcB8Q56LcqIpkcsmFVHY3MPLdKtjD-Kirh6axng" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Bridge of Agrippa, Rome.<br><br>Northernmost bridge across the Tiber in Augustan Rome, which connected the Campus Martius to the N Trans Tiberim plain and its suburban villas. <br><br>All but unknown from ancient texts, the pons may have carried Agrippa’s Aqua Virgo across the Tiber to supply water to Trans Tiberim, and perhaps especially to the vast Augustan villa known as the “Villa Farnesina” .<br><br>Following the discovery of a Claudian cippus that marked the limits of public property from the Trigarium to Pons Agrippae about 160 m upstream (i.e., N) of the Ponte Sisto, four concrete foundation piers for a bridge across the Tiber were found near the same location and were subsequently identified as the Pons Agrippae. The selce concrete used in these foundations has parallels in the foundations of the Thermae of Agrippa and in an Augustan vault of the Cloaca Maxima. Further, an Augustan tomb at the Transtiberine bridgehead was apparently erected “as an immediate consequence” of the construction of the bridge.]]></description>
