      <Placemark>
        <name>Porta Ostiensis (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gx8kAFkiZET-Gescczoe71NrdnsZGXRNR_UttBx9ZZtB1ijxM8RTCdxsPiXr9OehzZ3molG510Xpt2eZl0xZ_EuIHuS0TRL1qMqtNgdO8qEqINoH2uzPxihcMu7QinUyCj-7A5_BeieexB9q8S0KLld1zaPBCpW0fbaXAeOgvhVsk3Rikc0_YiWbAAnUNUMgBLlPP4nyeD7jA?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Aurelian Walls, Rome.<br><br>The original name of the gate was Porta Ostiensis, because it was located at the beginning of via Ostiense, the road that connected Rome and Ostia. Via Ostiense was an important arterial road, as evidenced by the fact that upon entering the gate of the same name, the road split, with one direction leading to the famous Emporium, the great market of Rome.<br><br>The gatehouse is flanked by two cylindrical towers, and has two entrances, which had been covered by a second, single-opening gate, built in front of the first by the Byzantine general Belisarius (530s–540s AD).<br><br>The structure is due to Maxentius, in the 4th century, but the two towers were heightened by Honorius. Its original — Latin — name was Porta Ostiensis, since it opened on the way to Ostia. Later, it was renamed to the Italian Porta San Paolo, because it was the exit of Rome that led to the Basilica of St. Paul Outside the Walls.<br><br>In 549 AD, Rome was under siege; the Ostrogoths of Totila entered through this gate, because of the treason of the Isaurian garrison. <br><br>On 10 September 1943, two days after the armistice between the Allies and Italy had been agreed, Italian military and civil forces tried to block German seizure of the city, with 570 casualties.<br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gx5_fPiZQHHQSciA8IMCMZQL2GWddfR2TWo0wZZkkcz_iwDh9SyxRJg4UL7NONRJ7_UdHCiPyyadcwO3vocJeRXlcjtcQci_IWaTdDBKZ1n-R8QaDTKVJqkG0FA8fDgDQIIXHegCFbcUnPBlo4geuL5j_pTeoLc58sWhpxPJA4AO0v3F4oZXiH__yUZ_gFbh87KX2RZk2fjMaQ?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1598-A52714</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gx8kAFkiZET-Gescczoe71NrdnsZGXRNR_UttBx9ZZtB1ijxM8RTCdxsPiXr9OehzZ3molG510Xpt2eZl0xZ_EuIHuS0TRL1qMqtNgdO8qEqINoH2uzPxihcMu7QinUyCj-7A5_BeieexB9q8S0KLld1zaPBCpW0fbaXAeOgvhVsk3Rikc0_YiWbAAnUNUMgBLlPP4nyeD7jA?authuser=0&fife=s16383 https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gx5_fPiZQHHQSciA8IMCMZQL2GWddfR2TWo0wZZkkcz_iwDh9SyxRJg4UL7NONRJ7_UdHCiPyyadcwO3vocJeRXlcjtcQci_IWaTdDBKZ1n-R8QaDTKVJqkG0FA8fDgDQIIXHegCFbcUnPBlo4geuL5j_pTeoLc58sWhpxPJA4AO0v3F4oZXiH__yUZ_gFbh87KX2RZk2fjMaQ?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
