      <Placemark>
        <name>Porta Praenestina (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GwHgVChCK9vi3oRtz6kMwI0JcIKnjXhgqar4G8BHSLHNpntmYXXC3J2PcublxVqacgsl06c1dLKQYjSe_B4h3ITwMXOQYpfGnMiVFyz4LFz8tG0VFD_hDIwfFqXF3VEgx6eXAEqAJVthyvnwpg3DWb6pSr1NKNGARPti6yhvWvRPvpyhKofiYheiZmXF2OmtiV9lRrN0I-r0g?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Aurelian Walls, Rome.<br><br>The Porta Maggiore, as it came to be known later, is by far the best urban site to visit for an understanding and view of the ancient aqueducts. It is a monumental double archway built of white travertine. It was first known as the Porta Prenestina, perhaps a reference to the road over which is passes (the Via Praenestina). The "gate," built in 52 AD by the emperor Claudius, was originally intended to provide a decorative section of support for two aqueducts, the Aqua Claudia and the Anio Novus. At that time these aqueducts crossed the ancient Via Labicana and Praenestina roads thereby providing the opportunity to create at this location a sort of triumphal arch to the conquest of nature and its conqueror, the emperor Claudius. The two channels of these aqueducts, (the Aqua Claudia and Aqua Anio Novus), one lying on top of the other, can be seen when viewing the cross-section running through the travertine attic at the top of the gate.<br><br>The gate was incorporated in the Aurelian Wall in 271 by the emperor Aurelian thus truly turning it into an entrance (gate) to the city. Experts refer to this as an early example of “architectural recycling,” essentially adapting one existing structure, to another use. In this case using an aqueduct as a wall.<br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gy38Xt_R4LjBL1rcmRdXATM3nIDUSCo-D29OBbBOxV2IUdUnx5gV-aIFpR6x7i0rp6Cc5MTKgEwA5FQN6o2g-cN-l8hxmkEzB2EIYN_Jou69IInOpUVdRGmWw_FeXeU3yA1W1zs-YS4DrRHjKWJOKJRPY5AqT-YqmD8h-Eir72D4SSWFsM1couzvfD37ZrMiELQkl1wvkByOA?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1598-A52714</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GwHgVChCK9vi3oRtz6kMwI0JcIKnjXhgqar4G8BHSLHNpntmYXXC3J2PcublxVqacgsl06c1dLKQYjSe_B4h3ITwMXOQYpfGnMiVFyz4LFz8tG0VFD_hDIwfFqXF3VEgx6eXAEqAJVthyvnwpg3DWb6pSr1NKNGARPti6yhvWvRPvpyhKofiYheiZmXF2OmtiV9lRrN0I-r0g?authuser=0&fife=s16383 https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gy38Xt_R4LjBL1rcmRdXATM3nIDUSCo-D29OBbBOxV2IUdUnx5gV-aIFpR6x7i0rp6Cc5MTKgEwA5FQN6o2g-cN-l8hxmkEzB2EIYN_Jou69IInOpUVdRGmWw_FeXeU3yA1W1zs-YS4DrRHjKWJOKJRPY5AqT-YqmD8h-Eir72D4SSWFsM1couzvfD37ZrMiELQkl1wvkByOA?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
