      <Placemark>
        <name>Porta Quirinalis (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GxQtA1b8zr04Qtjve5ymDhPwFfVTEVoot0iyYsUhlEtJrTqw_4_HXm0XIvcw7P7JX8nmn4PzGbRcLJ2qs6HJqRBqBsC8vqpNB7--HyzXaoS5mCOJg2S6Qg2gAAjurTqlQe_8Vpk6M5YUAhK5UCNMHqJvN1wvxZYWJqR4_pzG-zPNNzAnAINtQW7hNNmNzLqCYr1FvAoEQh6OQ?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Servian Walls. Rome.<br><br>Gate in the Servian Wall along the steep N slope of the Quirinal, located near the present-day Via della Quattro Fontane. No architectural remains survive and the position of the gate is estimated based upon the hypothetical path of the Servian Wall and several preserved sections of road.<br><br> The name derives from the nearby sacellum Quirini. Lanciani reports that remains of stairs were seen during excavations in 1892; these cappellaccio steps in opus quadratum may have been associated with the gate.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1598-A52714</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GxQtA1b8zr04Qtjve5ymDhPwFfVTEVoot0iyYsUhlEtJrTqw_4_HXm0XIvcw7P7JX8nmn4PzGbRcLJ2qs6HJqRBqBsC8vqpNB7--HyzXaoS5mCOJg2S6Qg2gAAjurTqlQe_8Vpk6M5YUAhK5UCNMHqJvN1wvxZYWJqR4_pzG-zPNNzAnAINtQW7hNNmNzLqCYr1FvAoEQh6OQ?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
