      <Placemark>
        <name>Porta Sanqualis (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gxho6ls0cReSuTe_4Je-b3SSwZXXT9sAsQpj4W1Emq612CV1-7NLQarNNJWmATy6GbZS5zH8MlPBRPHE7FPyIaMu7K_5DyNQMDA3AUG47InQx36UjaiRf7z3v0tZFtUb3XTgMHEaskwu1bcnXvuOtchv0un4F-_BZnX-l4ShNCFMuBz3P1EriAR9C1zpF16uHujBh2W5dmcpg?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Servian Walls. Rome.<br><br>Gate in the Servian Wall, located on the Quirinal near the Temple of Didius Fidius. The limited remains of the gate which survive in the vicinity of Largo Magnanapoli indicate that it had an elongated rectangular plan with an enclosed inner court.]]></description>
