      <Placemark>
        <name>Porta Settimiana (Rome, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GyruoBb86KfPrtrIntWSyHMKAcLRn_Y6kd5bZ55mdyrdAsInXcnWgwMMNPNTuqi6sgEtRlxA1vw6TPnK2z5FmWiFAGrSXelyuaANkmf6h25wCxghmf2VysysU4TP7NLcbfuPt-oZO7z-eOJZb3-E_vP4nWm8FFbLyVf5kFAfpPqjaubial0LzSca4aJxOZ2GyROfE72gokaTQ?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Aurelian Walls, Rome.<br><br>Porta Settimiana is one of the gates of the Aurelian walls in Rome. It rises at the northern vertex of the rough triangle traced by the town walls - built by Emperor Aurelian in the 3rd century - in the area of Trastevere an up through the Janiculum.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1598-A52714</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
