      <Placemark>
        <name>Porta Trigemina (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v7TuLzsbHbVXwhPgYC4dioSDJidvxsjL4L1J7pT10_Z-C8ZzjxuaCRoLXtw0YEdajUJorIp1mDdbDX-8Ykf0shvk1Ebw_h6CYQHSs4caukz71tTALmjOOXodqjow1S3Zd7_SN3diHgj2bgej_aPCjdDnZytKLpsINUKeWKfqpgacMTvARb2pv-dmABsyoUXZ0NHfPDYg4GwGywrGXFR7xNYj8MbBkhFYJb6frpPwMO6m1KWgE_hZoZU6lq6yAEGvTfyqgm90bG0WM0Pb_t0Nnmx8qjil-Ak3-RbvyskEup-tElmbkCtZEux7Ba8IG1AC34XWCOGwNql1aLkPKtz0k4RCuAGWqa-89n69QsuNS2iGuqKZO7SE-CK0Yu-6In2h-B4zYoX0nEHdHerNejNkx1Qr5Lu5u-sUio8zBrZYAA_XiYRYBdR3JkINUAQbuBHV0DPEHn9giS6JgHrHggXn9NhrYhL3cSVdheKi2wna7P0t5xZd7q4AV-V76LpYlkOx4b3NvgQ88CKKz1pxOp294QBM4c_4s-vs_4iM5fd93_UFVgAfVTBCncCQCRVDZ9sUuz45EiUVgWgZo3hcZlDyo3zt0LWjTQMJAgZ66j9yevJwGZ0bBwLEvqnwNvdMZLBOOqZqgLYbc2pfI68gtd4ut9xn7tpHRDFfIELBEhcEB_4kTJxrX1JTxCe0WZ3PuBoGU-GpPuSq8lJ" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Servian Walls. Rome.<br><br>Important ‘Triple Gate’ in the Republican defenses along the Tiber bank, located somewhere between the S Forum Bovarium and the N tip of the Aventine, at the lower end of the Clivus Publicius.<br><br> A gate of longstanding significance, the Porta Trigemina is mentioned both in connection with work commissioned for the Emporium in 174 BC, and as an area by the late-antique Regionary Catalogues. While this gate apparently functioned as the primary S gate in the section of the Servian Wall along the river, its location remains hypothetical. The remnants of a wall and an arch blocked with reticulate masonry are likely to have been in its vicinity. Lyngby’s suggested identification with the remains of a Grotta Oscura pylon further S along the Tiber bank has, for good reasons, not been accepted by subsequent scholarship.<br><br>Most agree that the “Arcus Lentuli et Crispini” is an Augustan renewal of the Porta Trigemina in the form of a monumental arch. Erected in 2 AD under the consuls P. Lentulus Scipio and T. Quinctius Crispinus Valerianus on a site between the S Forum Bovarium and the N tip of the Aventine, potentially on the same spot as the Porta Trigemina, it was destroyed in the 15th c. Since the wording of the dedicatory inscription coincides exactly with that of the “Arcus Dolabellae et Silani” on the Caelian, and since there is a parallel case of Augustan rebuilding, the “Fornix Augusti”, by the bridgehead of the *Pons Aemilius, Coarelli has plausibly discerned a large-scale Augustan program of converting the old city gates into monumental arches. The Porta Trigemina renewed as the Arch of Lentulus and Crispinus may be depicted in a lost relief recorded in the Codex Coburgensis.<br><br>Materially, the Arch of Lentulus and Crispinus seems to have replaced the earlier gate, yet since ‘Porta Trigemina’ is attested as a late-antique toponym, our map offers a single index number to represent both. The number is placed at the hypothetical site of the juncture between the Republican circuit wall and the street artery parallel to the river, which led from the S Forum Bovarium to the Emporium.<br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GzYiLlb2xSm9MjJg2KqE1S6VTobanqo6IlloUEtEKlJm1EinwmldMQwVhSAV6RRPdR4xZ3HLnCu69DYfQv1hYbL3eKOrqsWsZMc1OyjtkunGCA9FQwyIwWiMfFiNrDov_eC5ZrTbi1FblEdJJ1yv_UMmr5ypHOc8iig7v2aIM67JAAzP6ioHnIFuUm-fQZEqI7OKltBM9BCSA?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1598-A52714</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v7TuLzsbHbVXwhPgYC4dioSDJidvxsjL4L1J7pT10_Z-C8ZzjxuaCRoLXtw0YEdajUJorIp1mDdbDX-8Ykf0shvk1Ebw_h6CYQHSs4caukz71tTALmjOOXodqjow1S3Zd7_SN3diHgj2bgej_aPCjdDnZytKLpsINUKeWKfqpgacMTvARb2pv-dmABsyoUXZ0NHfPDYg4GwGywrGXFR7xNYj8MbBkhFYJb6frpPwMO6m1KWgE_hZoZU6lq6yAEGvTfyqgm90bG0WM0Pb_t0Nnmx8qjil-Ak3-RbvyskEup-tElmbkCtZEux7Ba8IG1AC34XWCOGwNql1aLkPKtz0k4RCuAGWqa-89n69QsuNS2iGuqKZO7SE-CK0Yu-6In2h-B4zYoX0nEHdHerNejNkx1Qr5Lu5u-sUio8zBrZYAA_XiYRYBdR3JkINUAQbuBHV0DPEHn9giS6JgHrHggXn9NhrYhL3cSVdheKi2wna7P0t5xZd7q4AV-V76LpYlkOx4b3NvgQ88CKKz1pxOp294QBM4c_4s-vs_4iM5fd93_UFVgAfVTBCncCQCRVDZ9sUuz45EiUVgWgZo3hcZlDyo3zt0LWjTQMJAgZ66j9yevJwGZ0bBwLEvqnwNvdMZLBOOqZqgLYbc2pfI68gtd4ut9xn7tpHRDFfIELBEhcEB_4kTJxrX1JTxCe0WZ3PuBoGU-GpPuSq8lJ https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GzYiLlb2xSm9MjJg2KqE1S6VTobanqo6IlloUEtEKlJm1EinwmldMQwVhSAV6RRPdR4xZ3HLnCu69DYfQv1hYbL3eKOrqsWsZMc1OyjtkunGCA9FQwyIwWiMfFiNrDov_eC5ZrTbi1FblEdJJ1yv_UMmr5ypHOc8iig7v2aIM67JAAzP6ioHnIFuUm-fQZEqI7OKltBM9BCSA?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
          </Data>
