      <Placemark>
        <name>Porta Viminalis (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GwJJsLJDmDLzG2W38O7CQit92ZBMunHbpbasDO9sFxrn-K2HBdADhgMslAb8AlQyIuMEXXQ5kPe61c4SVy-HKuvWsNvhaIYvvlC9AH1PMP3Pvm91fOhBwMiEqIr9cp9E4CQf6bxoEanYVs83KPjhDZ7uPddK3V9QZ99wuLbruJW_cNCa2h5rgUPighcfh1Uw7Xo69FmQThkTA?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Servian Walls. Rome.<br><br>Gate in the Servian Wall on the Viminal, between the Porta Collina and Porta Esquilina. It connects the Vicus Collis Viminalis with the “Via Tiburtina Vetus”. <br><br> Part of this gate has been discovered in front of the Termini train station in the shape of two converging walls in opus quadratum of peperino (from Gabii). These were part of the side walls of the gate, not just retaining walls for a trapezoidal opening in the Agger. The ground-plan may be reconstructed following Säflund. A line of aqueducts (Aqua Iulia, Aqua Tepula, Aqua Marcia) passed on the N side of the gate into the city.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1598-A52714</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GwJJsLJDmDLzG2W38O7CQit92ZBMunHbpbasDO9sFxrn-K2HBdADhgMslAb8AlQyIuMEXXQ5kPe61c4SVy-HKuvWsNvhaIYvvlC9AH1PMP3Pvm91fOhBwMiEqIr9cp9E4CQf6bxoEanYVs83KPjhDZ7uPddK3V9QZ99wuLbruJW_cNCa2h5rgUPighcfh1Uw7Xo69FmQThkTA?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
