      <Placemark>
        <name>Porticus Minucia (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v5loEzyY5wJT14WeCddNi1_F_4Rxn2tgjZ6epycPKliWrZMKGIL41kVpbq8GYU5XTyM1VZivEtXnoXnKsVCny-ZiZfybfc49uG-IyZqIICG4sPikPnHpKYAOhCz2hG1lsj7vPmSYgfXrzCSbG4zyDicLoJw16NNqqyRaqHonJ7XlMD1tR5M0GyNRq9NiY0y_Tyr7e4COFQwgDNFr1PwwBOTloQpvk_6l_qCBeLLabwDoz_3Lp3YJ9AtHvE8SXQo2eCEadso4aaR7k2PyaNp00AWJqz_oIrASQgqTSm836B7CakkxhNtg_lXS-sHOPptBTdgrvh0OXHDIKNy49AQx5vdfv563q7-m6WwubfUmUVV03WchgXpxVn2Iaagp3vMY3MyjDqi03-BlRurfwxvyiUshidsGATXwkHhOpGAf0DKnlubKGRdzkClOpHIqcsggxEN-5PPW294jF-QcHsCJWIosa5LGcY-EbDIeolNrIjmb_9RtxUSYHAJgIo3HhFuD8feQUtlpTJvOaEwE0d9q6lhgIPtbGXYjCntdA83WL3QDNf3NVg8tfniqTIykMdnmZW17omA9Du_K9SCKcOgLYa8yc_Iz1-Lv5XUGwveBphAKiX0TRurUbNGE10oLasxELammIXQRTEMBn_E1Suj1FKqX9x9Vv40HRMMkf65iByhGUGewNJl8bW5WKrd5N2HSbyMN2Zp5-ZPXw" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Portico of Minucius, Rome.<br><br>Celebrated portico in the S Campus Martius, built in the last decade of the 2nd c. BC by M. Minucius Rufus; its colonnade encircled the earlier Temple of the Lares Permarini. The 4th-c. AD Regionary Catalogues list it in Regio IX: Circus Flaminius between the Porticus Philippi and the Crypta Balbi. The portico is shown in just that location on the Severan Marble Plan, where it is labeled MINI[CIA].]]></description>
