      <Placemark>
        <name>Thermae Traiani (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GwVria62QUD53nDymBdY-XQxpadv-rj9MGt0oM7I78VPy30NIaHLvWrmTLeAoc16A9Fl-Mh1ZSz2stMkVlKvVbzFD0DO4L2XCCeHcrS7-5SV-maQfSkgUzpOzMA9MMd7GJdUQL3_Ha0d7HVe5xvgQSnVfQp1r82taanL93l5VSzGLpLrb6W93OHnPMFHwh8rSF96B6xEzclEA?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Baths of Trajan, Rome.<br><br>The Baths of Trajan were a massive thermae, started in 104 AD and dedicated during the Kalends of July in 109 AD.<br><br> Commissioned by Emperor Trajan, the complex of baths occupied space on the southern side of the Oppian Hill on the outskirts of what was then the main developed area of the city, although still inside the boundary of the Servian Wall. The architect of the complex is said to be Apollodorus of Damascus. The baths were being utilized mainly as a recreational and social centre by Roman citizens, both men and women, as late as the early 5th century.<br><br> The complex seems to have been deserted soon afterwards as a cemetery dated to the 5th century (which remained in use until the 7th century) has been found in front of the northeastern exedra. The baths were thus no longer in use at the time of the siege of Rome by the Ostrogoths in 537 AD; with the destruction of the Roman aqueducts, all thermae were abandoned, as was the whole of the now-waterless Mons Oppius. Early Christian writers misnamed the remains the 'Baths of Domitian'.<br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GzB7gEkk34-3B0xLZ_aRUMHnO1WbJRer7XBG9DkJXAfK55pyeWE_UKMB4cAFxvtL4of1NHvaO-yzhNxzm3mnIhqQ_WYRuZ-x4snP3TUKkNdWLkmunHrtigMPyTzSohBSA45RVxAItac1lSKzJlsew89_n8A9SG1UddVv3k65XXK4WmEViEAdY_5UQrHlAH8HfZu1ELR_Ew0gg?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gw9TLCF6k5Hc514jLndh47mHVcs8u2WYU7d_bCu3-29i8WMXpD6bqYea47bbKM4U3Qx5R8BGfqEDCbcjbaTX8k7ogtFNYH-FwzwR4eWHbwfufVaCPvcQtm0lWH6C_YI4P6BwwDOs-bGcsm6FfwGZp3fgb2tCHhO-RWOZ-HNPCdDdvQMLo7263Vi0AQSyWs6qsSFGW2N52SPlw?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
