        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GwfLqPrT4P9v8XPTaGCWPqFH2q25j6wEuTtSQa0cmJtsE2duiShqA9bJVSe9S3wvfxxKR2xMir6xG4kZ8gGi5PeSMepSzUs_-yZnOfKkWIJR5P9_Zx2-_c3CrVCRI4zyWolK-3PuY3c_Jhoug1AghAhiUKTM-GnyZARfDuqqu19d8wt0HhO9KTlkTYw6RhUCLKBPEhhjeWQwgE?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Aurelian Wall Tower, Rome.<br><br>The Aurelian Walls were constructed between 270 and 275 AD at the behest of the Emperor Aurelian, as a defence for the city from the threatened invasion of barbarians from the North of Europe. The new enclosing wall had a perimeter of about 19 km and was constructed of sections of wall about 6.5m in hieght, with a parapet walkway along the top, punctuated every thirty metres by higher towers, covered by terraces.]]></description>
