      <Placemark>
        <name>Amphitheatrum Flavium (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v7CxFiGmMXlteDwPy7lNHaVZ9_VhM5auVG3KEiuZYyiuNQvqjnixjO48P53dgvbbKteSiYx8P4jXiwWShC9R6UivxmtEO84wflscGRxWKY8xSqhfCcb2-55jixT0svpQsnurO70GcY2zSsCdly1YNbU95lwaRg-OnZ0UQOXXi3uZijMcBKGBaAREXWEzgzlE9dFrtGu9FbI9jghLFpTtbzLQvuoG8_JaCt3XWQVPaOs_8F6Cc5FjzB3dWR-kZbUGdUtIGfOICPWK8dW3Ka-kx8KDDVDm22vO0c4Za6AJQLbAsvrDO1Zrouvl5FlI9_Kix7AqbYC6pItAgRNgdZGBJB6XncIqKO3qT6GC5PWs7Z7LzhJLhf0XWZskyONzDTkN8AeFKSwVPhDeQu4LaIbLdBcMMjSmw6yR4Zm35wc-bdU622g2qah8v7Unpl6g9dxJkuPm2_KkfKnADSz3XXTiG0g3nH6920-x1HBXrf60zazvJFAb4Fi5ieKtlGUFDLyQoMXcF04gs_vT2f_dlNr6e66RmJwThOXKzGYgEm0WLqPT4eu_yUlKJ1oYRav3G_4N1KCc825fuK3yxMQLdGDW0qo4rSiPKUmljozh1vyWd7q4KQZRpqBWwQSL_c24-diKYoyGGaWEHRHKREMlgP2KyzY3wwGXxxV5MBGpz3CW91KPCK6kL6ZuwNaU6HmtUig_X048HVL5xATyQ" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Colosseum, Rome.<br><br>The Flavian Amphitheatre is an oval amphitheatre in the centre of Rome. Built of travertine, tuff, and brick-faced concrete, it is the largest amphitheatre ever built. The Colosseum is situated just east of the Roman Forum. <br><br>Construction began under the emperor Vespasian in 72 AD, and was completed in 80 AD under his successor and heir Titus. Further modifications were made during the reign of Domitian. These three emperors are known as the Flavian dynasty, and the amphitheatre was named in Latin for its association with their family name (Flavius).<br><br>The Colosseum could hold, it is estimated, between 50,000 and 80,000 spectators, having an average audience of some 65,000; it was used for gladiatorial contests and public spectacles such as mock sea battles (for only a short time as the hypogeum was soon filled in with mechanisms to support the other activities), animal hunts, executions, re-enactments of famous battles, and dramas based on Classical mythology. The building ceased to be used for entertainment in the early medieval era. <br><br>It was later reused for such purposes as housing, workshops, quarters for a religious order, a fortress, a quarry, and a Christian shrine.<br><br><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v5tBDDKCiY5ambBfkQzQo52OjntghrHh9w78neSsyGCX6fNR2FFvIwC55DM1a-F7uh39iK8LcXO4wGSr4ZUSHUxXhVCn2qJH04QXbHq7Fwk4HrvBE9zwvoVGmIXTARGd57ZZ3mLLhLVC8fXolntTHAvpuQ6l9_DUXp174HN22ffuSapwNebx-hT0ou0jne_s8toVqNGFVPbTd7n-6hseTnifV3g0O2pRKGmvRGSQIWmLypIkQBhRt6YoamYYxtVEar86jdcRPSLY-QRrNyqljWm5kpzV8vIimNR01-9S099K6i460XHEykfFLKmfxyo7SMUpoNlnJxgTc3LeMGCyCe_dG9chNXeTrkykrp__sY9Xb3XohtGb6Ag3UbtEqe-7qUN62vSGE8NJ2E2i2_YaX1WszPTaHuzLyvMxncPf_lPmV43q_yvtXr1Xi81g4NKs5r4TkBq-C2QoSmqvpiQPamhdtIpDbuaC4-tsS9e0a0GCEZUt6Dfl1aQcuP9_30ueU5HoIK-wjM5gW0aKYvqkD6FbPM1iz1KTseWLxekqhhkLRPuefpMAQd1Vty1ZMPqhM7D2gMACjwN_gt-HB64BtkoQkfNtnJXdwLlDF33wRllOWHw6CB3xLnsqVFCJMmlkX_cxPDIAs3FB8ob9xJKIANrWeRCOWkYUsGIMK1WQJEpV1-fxh_uoAD341fdFDzCWox_KBLpo9saMw" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v4rTqtPWE1bp2zdBNSEoDPSh1pwqMmLQeoEKNBIWWLr79BzH19QScr6fl3CgmgYkM7Fho1aF8xGKAlsY-V0dgX1fpsX8shatMg6m9Q1Ym-z6JFcHwsdReGjvZU13UHSLa9LSQldaRZsrKSbyUBRRVAI3wpf2q4GpH437MzeFEbo6IRM71TLFt_1zzp6z8j_9WeYL2Usz8M0BmUDs3H25LYEEPOoLfdeoVnTQufmUaWF1-3OkR4LNzDnQmhvZ7TmcSqJo1GyXbMBgT5OUF6bt0o4IetWtIUCE7NEF31Be-8W35GgmR_DlLCHzmdVkjpAW_W0KzpIuwvy0t1InfG-UGTtjEZuEUn_DtbpjXdVEa4DssDtzMSC2A_cBFJzCMwG6mNGfno5DJUNIg-F4D1Ea_ZORaI3NPuZtou4AWwGHprwF_s9_IR2AoxAt_YGtXjTjTOiRLwVu7_HSMO87PIBQaib21Yax0b3gqv4pawG0K7evqbf97sPFAWWJHQP7rMDTvX2vBGSTBI0y7d251AVQsQpP9M7Tou7JzC8waNMwVa5NgMOv4hReIQq3bDjJgLw4Vgf5LhLHnyL4jhT-rloddYe7wojngcL1ys8aEK0SsLCZT1MEisyK_gCTzqQg59ryjKq0JSpez124FsLpYlig9OPzIjd6sTQanUUK2kW9mmsEmThvMbuXtaSb9M3HeAYLPdXd-PmUBViTA" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v5lWkioZnhv3womweTlAzyxGWP-kraXBLI4QjkizUYl0kXs_t_sDRcvfgYo5mqG5bCWss30fPh_4vk8WUHfoUXg6D-ff3YXqRo53g8XtQST_luGYxJ-HZ53Cv5Ke-U4tYWLa4A7EBstddhb2h1Zt2irBavw1yK7pMeUDahtNPeoEYnMp8M-w4TqOalvK0kc_9m1KcVyUfhqw6aYYxjH8oWDiGtGFDytum9rrSbLml0LJw3Ckm355xbjH