      <Placemark>
        <name>Amphitheatrum Statilii Tauri (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v4JTke-gDM3NP_Wlvl_9XT4NB7_nGwFongemgOk0PXcgxYCAv1mW5n3y2GYYC1_pKXBysT4GEqV0pnDvkbbLYAEgGYTla4sTO1vEpnAhRllglCg9vNfi5huumxwd5NHt9Ck0sEa4EmmeHkiqp0wcMQRQPAwP6TOyDou-7VV9dsMqzb6PqVeKM3U8K5oPTU5NQoXcPcoUepOy6bGuNCVyiYIechrfYscU2JRZX4rRDPka-AcYrPfpwBD2XNxwFaSF4v3ls4FAO-iI2MMUGQlxNA0gZKnzS4PzoHFMK1yTJehU8rOKhdPPdxZTGdMfw1RiPX86jFO9WbRBCoswyRzCUMYIB9jZpzuUw_g2Xk32wXEIeL9ZTRDJyzFujwPetznp3Vm4r-M6NAYdDc7UX4xrFwh9drwo9DrIp_7QOZQbZFELwlHvCzURkmxGiHQy2hiUqd1y3PqhXGdt9LLpWldlniGQmhgVUyULd-ORJvFbkoTakVS4FLmJsv6AOQ8aK_JCOpp23Yeebykglp5TSoBpCA6_0Eh-Sj1dQgUXgH2ZVw3Q9PuCBH1065_fJnVf7urT8b80Ip32nMw0JQF_evbsdSX_A_GNUfQraKPMr_MnPyCHZDL9eCV7lc4yqdb7x_B2AaTrSgFbxEmy51McMUG3aFntmfZqm7ETwTn5YqHujcmcTai22AS2zLxzaYAiUEuIqntDDcCsNV2" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Amphitheatre of Statilius Taurus, Rome.<br><br>T. Statilius Taurus built the first stone amphitheatre in Rome, which he dedicated in 29 BC. <br><br>This private amphitheater may not have been very large, as it was often passed over for important imperial spectacles. In 64 AD fire destroyed the theatre, which was probably built in large part of wood; consequently its location within the Campus Martius remains a matter of speculation.<br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GzjQOy9AnYDs4--zK8LFvK8GaVHxxQhjwaWKE-RGi4evV4QyyIrSu8n61R3ABQqrnnwzXbPEtASaNmWMDjAcpQympCEKhYXXk81TUhjoDuqveukSy-NVVJ_TBjHqvX9IHLk7RMwV1hnqNwXziqQNoLVFS5x5p8NonKjGrOgOOQV2tO_JFxjtTBJ38ULANx1b2rmdN6pHUPApg?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1788-A52714</styleUrl>
