      <Placemark>
        <name>Athenaeum Hadriani (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v7ZRJAkYKpwjqW4UVZNhBfnkdkbdpE9NMUDNq_dxguBURl27yhhSy37DMOQRujjezBAQ1iw9VjBrI75c9NbkurUxkXMKW5ep--h6PSGz2WQAj_8AWnhyPu8-HR3xnGSNifXyZD7G3QIGfmCEr8Vjj2MDNhUS_cd5Uxe4-3ON9VrbPi_ykYiezWOt8g9ltibjKzFrVhhkaUimYugxz6fMVc-5nFpB-yw8WytOyb7bFqHR5s0r7BTCh4jEIWZd6yRYRAyRYCUzsjFShq0K6mwYTw0ulaqFIFIHNf_jOTR83B07-x-V9mxotTATn0pBX3cZt5uP3moQ3jiAY47QqxW5bukVdvKr8nhxgjC09_yRyrjrF5gAmywy6rR5_u0pyZH8MODVhCufnYznXCCrAteRJdGyfQsmrKoJyMcOwquJN3cR5Ln9OzdUsfpZOTRVzyPe0DEka6DDFBNketCh5Zs_ciXgoO-q3RX-1ZEJX-4vAZcnAc_YpU9xLGfZQbc-B6HftCesGHLMVB5VrpIdVzOPJWe6UD0nTuqh0p8pudF8WIqnG5-rqgZdtciyBBeyAXBlmLfnJvJ-xEj81sA7eETH3KYFTt-I9U5y2lpArIceIpJSWnZIzaVaWzZ7FCXlwFjtO8foJsWXp0mmYnJ3QRJVJ8-qTWqds3Ngqn-a13LA0d1SwLLt-4YG3Jij_qOINGz3PFwFioaK5073w" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Intellectual school of Hadrian, Rome.<br><br>The Athenaeum was a school (ludus) founded by the Emperor Hadrian in Rome, for the promotion of literary and scientific studies (ingenuarum artium) and called Athenaeum from the city of Athens, which was still regarded as the seat of intellectual refinement. The Athenaeum was situated near the Capitoline Hill: its site was discovered in 2009 during excavation for the construction of the Rome Metro C Line, in the middle of what is now Piazza Venezia.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1709-A52714</styleUrl>
