      <Placemark>
        <name>Circus Flaminius (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v4oAGd1Nu5nUqGFnPSVSRr8CVJqYSJ4IBeNQ2t4_aN1jxtdClerDFVmaXDeSSuwrQK7O6bkoKUuACtJ8_J8HkgGFmfRqAXp6hmQTPFGjf_Qod_8-ZHboJS_RzKA6zX7RGn6K6tNG-ka2Z-B48jleU5WC9npW8_NtEuxf17BjLLVESKBAfT7ZbwsqGQ-tlkbu8YqIWmvfHRfPhwjVYXjrdyhUPcJxw8kn6WCRv8LcfqA0gYI0bMPUHWNU0GpERjV1rBFnmZk78dGJBVLCVUv_DRc7MvhV1odPZs6c0QQkp6xHN-AE-zNwm_wcql1x6T13D2JjwIYwOHEeXAPRGsw3G920LdjTdjxoSMV0St1gBhfV8YSVXbDJWihIsa8nniBljThtk7h-leRQmcmConLWnjdcT9xNX9Zwnke-pIB5aX3GH-yju3YJ9yJ00QFUqX1gwxufr0bu23z9NKn4ObYUHhe--EZkphqbt8GLY4yBpEFxNXvRy8gexxhy1Cy1-eRPsoT4ZrP6CEiWxRRWZ-nMplIUMXZYYA8zUUIBrJ7OJig15oApwBSwFFCsrzCRCQl_shR_EZczdW9-bOKI5qNXLOZb42M6pfNhuEuxUvaBbgAa_9_RxPykQeklrzaieYzcJcRRhbY6x53DNJWfqB0HCS_ufYxen2_OI-p0_WhuM8J1h-OG-lt3YNtDAXyAUEeKdl37YucWoagzg" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Race track, Rome.<br><br>Large open space — not a formal circus — in the SW Campus Martius, between the Theatrum Marcelli and the Temple of Mars, and oriented along the NW axis of the road which led to the Tiber and beyond that, to Veii. <br><br>The area was topographically significant since it gave its name, sometime after the Augustan era, to Regio IX: Circus Flaminius. The Circus Flaminius occupied the prata Flaminia, property donated to the people of Rome in 221 BC by C. Flaminius; however, the original property may not have corresponded exactly to the later extension of the circus. <br><br>The strong triumphal character of the Circus Flaminius is stressed by the high density of sacred structures (most of them victory monuments) — either identified through archaeological remains or mentioned in ancient accounts — that cluster around it and define its boundaries. While it is generally assumed that the long sides of the Circus were monumentalized by temples, there is no evidence that any sacral buildings other than the Temple of the Dioscuri delimited the SW side. In fact, the Marble Plan from the Via Anicia shows commercial horrea (warehouses) flanking the temple.<br><br><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v6ph2VdZRiypvDDqWJfUNFqtOvleJw0oxCGv9L4u2wLyDn1aw08uU7lDOzyPqmQFYsZ6iXv7RJz_VHitvKIuSJO9aOmkBm2aXHGaoya6tbUb_u8RXGWcXKEBMuqf70k41uT7EvVNzWbNgwHHpzy7Kw61V_vv1EnQLX8HMF0zCtNZW1fU-XjGern-ey9WV3ijOgjloQw3ZC9hVjBfviMqNUXxcy2zLIPUkZiFH7ICrSF-yWmkro0H8T2dtTLcIyH_5xRzpGgqSz0IF7fbTeCllYsOT3D57nuZAf1A1igar3gVY2mL6ug4p7w-l09ToomRS4FdXIxhIehGQp35kwydTfoiRopJIGMsQLt3TIKH2j62b12RKLKyKFU7dhbKex_Xsc5a4_cmTVYk1JekMl0j4N7XD7lcjDlzAjSnefVlg4t4XkgjJy7GR98dFlPOU8EjOzbYrxBUyvcjBCIso2p4GeYiqP-NU-tGhzqbW12LM5H13oXZHKSRGZF3DAwIZMX3Bk5uzvW1lh4turB45VZ-tZPsP1k4HMOAtw6lYEQNUROuItKwnq116UWLUqCskpqnyLTONLAau0_H4w_pimUt9roeVwEEgWOBkCaXGl9JY0lf1R2aSB7Ewn5t-DLKXigRqsMKT7qdtRTlIP_5k9Uc1JEZA5fjv65_fe5dyduFUvXRwkQPmoPBJLmbS70YMH5foLSeUGuulmI-A" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
