      <Placemark>
        <name>Circus Maxentii (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GwkxGyOVHb1dhuQ5mkh2vltDyFIIV3qyfrI8cj1-NaEVSnxPb14VFx68hIDPCFsUHFHoDteDKI3tbjsCf9Kq7Yltcd2U-fnuMp4sGEiCNGdVeK8nLjTDtg5SzDlfZH0S8MIbLq3e_iGLrzQSUjF2GU6NG3Zgy3GAFdh85FZPEIIdIrxITaZAYgLeGOuLxRuAQ2D83-Or-hXzA?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Race track of Maxentius, Rome.<br><br>The Circus of Maxentius is part of a complex of buildings erected by emperor Maxentius on the Via Appia between 306 and 312 AD. It is situated between the second and third miles of the Via Appia between the basilica and catacombs of San Sebastiano and the imposing late republican tomb of Caecilia Metella, which dominates the hill that rises immediately to the east of the complex. It is part of the Parco Regionale Appia Antica (Appian Way Regional Park).<br><br>The Circus itself is the best preserved in the area of Rome, and is second only in size to the Circus Maximus in Rome. The only games recorded at the circus were its inaugural ones and these are generally thought to have been funerary in character. They would have been held in honour of Maxentius' son Valerius Romulus, who died in 309 AD at a very young age and who was probably interred in the adjacent cylindrical tomb (tomb of Romulus). The imperial box (pulvinar) of the circus is connected, via a covered portico, to the villa of Maxentius, whose scant remains are today obscured by dense foliage, except for the apse of the basilical audience hall, which pokes out from the tree tops. The complex was probably never used after the death of Maxentius in 312 AD (archaeological excavations indicate the tracks were covered in sand already in antiquity).<br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GysiK5loptQPx4OKcbeDKjrLd8-bFEH1xbp3BnChKbvwsrl47CAn-wet7QAyK0Quyj3CjCWHRrTjjOAPhpy6HVr3aEEbuzg6pmlrylEdti6VP9s2bQdygDEIW8XF695cYNxXtnd1M8F7hQqPSAdhYNMYA-279S6C5dvV7W4drH0igT5CCQYlVc_o-qYYvhwAxehRShOz4veBw?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GwSWTs2UN0b85JWHdTgt12x4b8jcm155d89NBF9LcACThNZkUWFY63F0klQkT_gLx0mbx4iunhET9aVJ0zD1LoXaipQOPwcWVDcDoJ_7BGjxirRsO_cIX-nyzXuXO6r3fjNmO_mF6v0Z_Ur4gd9sjP7I7RKEPB_k4qDFvwTNbiBILP25oTf7GTQHjYLAbiM4iWZe3LIlgMnNw?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gyco-5AyPXGEqTWhWhSQ0qJW-piW3VY5N2Z64HJLvKb1cfIXTZVe7mil86PUSwpjILfLJ3EFaGmeUmDVprWAjQjoLTZbOcn4ObkUJkWpR8zISZav9-jl6PNp9xc95YfrjvlXqVWp8N6x1QqxG3mrn83j1ukL77N-YM3OZK9OBuvdiA1OguqraEX1dRfuHiQuYLqX-SbNxF3vw?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
