      <Placemark>
        <name>Circus Varianus (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gyory2qnUCo-yH-FUL3QO2ZFMtf9XgJz_84YSUGQq0ZlPVFU9ZDegXEvGUlOOPbEs2S1FTC3aGBt64Hi7KEc2Wm_6tumthEq1C1YnTO5_dSt8D7g1zBE36o4GIXenc87s3nhIvWSdKYyCZYNVQ6s4I2xdN3ctmjEb2dGWSYpxZfYdvHDQJu5ZCW2nNRnLcEToMnM0FUH1l9vA?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Race track, Rome.<br><br>The Circus Varianus was a circus, possibly started around the time of Caracalla, residing in the palatial villa complex known as the Sessorium, beside the Amphitheatrum Castrense. This circus has been identified as the space in which Elagabalus raced horses under the family name of Varius, lending the site the name of "Circus Varianus." The remnants of the circus survive to the south of Porta Maggiore, next to the Aurelian Wall, near the church of Santa Croce in Gerusalemme. The dimensions of the circus measure 565 x 125 meters, just slightly smaller than the Circus Maximus (600 x 150 m).<br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GzMwWkTWiLXdsHDWNkJUwHBfY7aJhVGkzb3hsCFhyUdrbZRXARP63ie0Y35eBvSffi1IKNjsC2O633C600q28DKYG47MDb62U28F0KtZU5WEmgtGIp-5MjaJYaJ0fJScRD5IWcmaZNAD6d8d2lydL-l0tY7gd-sCL0iUVyb0_YRnucOySK7pIua1YDjs5T_UB_o1grvLIDDpA?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GxPITT7nG2XGBYEuGf5RhUqNIcoNeHrrmarXU2CZEMaaKL4tl70MO7v3JEBMl-w5jqFD7r1D6VxW1K7D9X0xwCisfKGY6dHtnp7Lv-UD9HdapfWId5T-f7-stwoqPIUcHd95AR_X0b3HEWjQu0LiIrlQFLo9Q--_MKku5Ys-4lUJdcc4-e8dwAvTKzmjY91NVPPhkM0aQBmsQ?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
