      <Placemark>
        <name>Stabula Factionem (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v68ByHtQYJ1AOO1jDDscA_tDY61iEeYEraYbiE4XEYtkGPLxH5N6tB_DFTRK2fu8WB65WeAZGJs5jfPGKMvmyKfPLPE1AamD3v4rhkiJI6BlX1iucMI5dNctdMHMX8EIdQtVi9gNpKAozKbaZIBLKueUo-Y0KY5t_23KLLl3KKnOv7SIJ_O54lSTIqqYwRxLpFo8RlYU0NO8hTmCjpy1YuJfq5eX_owwlsTnX0hiZZdlvy7glbUvdmoLXtTSAgDPMsLiC3PuBYZcWnVSPU8yzp-u0v4LbHCtTfOWXFZ2b-kYke22YaZGOfdqymOFpFKFjdkw5BvSjusRegIU84id9O-Za63f-JLJOh0d0dYLKZNz-i26iNLOlQeRfvyEK2pc8pjcYtumuTcUWop6LcSocDe_auH6bG9Iazxm2NPGrDU4cuGlslDV-pJEfjRokVc1nCuppK5ktMC6KlYSHxGks_z2TbXE5GZ6Bf_BDr-CWjHHIjnZBoybcZ40Y3ko_DrHePUtnhPpkkyMRedTEXd-ZsvON61QhiFA5EZ3IjRfI5Za6j3-mkPl0oW18ksKZgN-pQn4BNGlIVU-kJAZzcYw6YXnlTfJuoGJ46PwP7nKUAKu69OjkobLmvEizB9oqed6GIIZmYD7Am7EzXjt6BlCI3PuHHA9W3N2EZ0xpoL0XqWHHTlezBk8roneKNCG--cx4I_CMAagpMmcw" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Stables of the Chariot Factions, Rome.<br><br>Stables for the horses belonging to the racing teams (factiones) in Rome, located in the W Campus Martius near the Trigarium. In the Augustan period there were four factiones: Albata, Prasina, Russea, and Veneta.<br><br>The factio Prasina was located near the Church of S. Lorenzo in Damaso, which retained the topographical attribute in its alternate mediaeval name: S. Laurentii in Prasino; an inscription mentioning the statio Prasina was found in situ nearby. About 50 m to the E, the possible remains of the factio Veneta were unearthed beneath Palazzo Regis and Palazzo Farnese. Although the locations of the other two factiones are unknown, several inscriptions found within a restricted area suggest that the two stables were located next to each other. Moreover, corroborating evidence for this location is offered by the existence of the V[ICVS STA]BLARIVS in this area.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1601-A52714</styleUrl>
