      <Placemark>
        <name>Theatrum Balbi (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v7Bky1ITsNGOw3N9SLJ2olE2mXN8Ab7iPtXfqMMQWvnqUfbKT_h39k4QrLgKfQuqLDouthfe4Qd8ArECiIuQdtmbWa5OMBHgQarj9aItwVdqBeSMmbPccoVhLp80cP_PSlSX7bOhRCRG1uMD212tZ3jsap5KJ3EDKToBWPMCh5UpdMiGDB-h8GQVPrk0v-WMj3acbTIyik-n-VUWlwV1FoK9b8z2N3sl2iWAMhcQH43oEUUOZX_TXs_ClJzVFQp2QamUMbj_kDdy3NOizTbb0PR5S1LlphuEqfmDurlKmcKRgKajS8t6oZPwPS8HNVMHHzrjmHf7pCUqlbg0Q_VcPSLYvmfBQhfaCYAcYRBe7iRdRjTRRCWIk56JF0oSxNrCtfwseBEF1pcuAhx4nB6A4MeZqADMlC_AgyLyNdU4i9MT6l3EFoCdjOB5EcY0iLbVHwvVN-nKQANvOhjxsbYHkhXNU1ixW3c3wh0tZogZQS5XusbVcUI8sk-LfZaup1JWnaNIRzVNj-6KlW3-qjNE9xBogQMYKEJISOLF5CzH1s8KlV5W6IIsncZAqmDR-T2HC8cQMoSpWhVa1I5MPy1Vst37vUdqpDNEm_n7T5Us1dL9yO-1ZzA1pQ8G9gNhMJkjYEviYgdWTfuceRKd488TTaSx0K0_7yMzmWig3jIbUOI6HX3HmVqhZTjdVjW_SMl00PXdf47Wwilyg" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Theatre of Balbus, Rome.<br><br>The smallest of the three stone theatres in Rome, built in the S Campus Martius by L. Cornelius Balbus (minor), probably after his triumph in 19 BC, as a part of the Augustan program of ‘adorning the city’.<br><br> It was dedicated in 13 BC during a flood of the Tiber, and stood S of the Porticus Minucia. Like the Theatrum Pompeium, the cavea of the Theatre of Balbus was oriented to face E. A number of its support walls in opus reticulatum have been preserved beneath Palazzo Mattei di Paganica. To the E of the stage building stood a large three-sided portico, which came to be known as the ‘crypta Balbi’. In the center of this portico stood a large rectangular structure of uncertain interpretation, which also seems to have been built by Balbus. The E portion of the complex is shown on the Severan Marble Plan and its remains are preserved near Via delle Botteghe Oscure. Excavations have shown that earlier residential buildings were destroyed to make room for the portico, and the region immediately to the E of the theatre contained a number of private structures by the time Augustan intervention began in this area.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1709-A52714</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
