      <name>Temples</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Ara Iovis Vinimi (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Altar of Jupiter Viminus, Rome.<br><br>Ancient altar to Iuppiter Viminus, the titular deity of the collis Viminalis, located on the Viminal.<br><br> An ancient drawing found in the excavations of Monte delle Giustizia, in the vicinity of the Porta Viminalis, depicts a cylindrical altar inscribed VIM resting on a rectangular plinth. A statue of Jupiter found near the point where Via Cavour joins Piazza dei Cinquecento may have been linked to the cult; yet it is of late-Imperial date and was not recovered in situ, so its value as evidence for the Augustan shrine is limited. Though the exact locale of the altar remains elusive, these two pieces of evidence suggest a location near the Porta Viminalis.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1548-9C27B0</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            12.499736,41.900501,0
