      <Placemark>
        <name>Ara Saturni (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v4Ni7QquecZ6GQLNA7kXpkHffCS4TqeDTejDxtyVcud-uK17s-oMu2fshxoBWDNK7ch1u0RUwXcR1JXgFjw_VLScNCjgyYuwlO8pxHh7nCNu2L7DrbtXuJd3og_fUsbvnMR5WXdiFVrrYjYcMbk7sOBcbHHLG34lB5mXQy888y96CR0tws_pigjLaxoKBCf9ai51P-P7WiSSjAfPBMoaEuwZ13fMoRKDOMCEgCrYFsM9FZ34A-6l2zXLkTMUqe0BDr4OkkxzmEAFlYhpD5s_fgpen1NlRpqZPhzjvBLx7Z1QcSTy65tLzed8JJW0NmMvXYJZrp6M4kfC1apw5XSTozWNvVu4Dbor7tPGWlFHxkymQrFs_vxW22xyjCRS7pvIznwOB3cO-eK2MANfz4-TIgXvC4UoSV-KPS5ao0tzY-joT3yF3_SnoE9f9mXjRe6losBj6DZzgedMFYQgrF8N5TfbSDdyOYcRh-RbjSkXOTI81Gtvs2eRFqYFF-WV9BVKVg-P2ryl5ld2oQjNlbcWNnchwDm9JbPDvqC0T6wVdNoQm9HkJQS2qi3zS4WW-M3LY4LHPBoqd2mrMYm-3QhmCIWwnTnpE3Z7M__aGW7ntLxBWNbSGwyP9d_8eUwRXlCZcUaquj5PHypT77s_dW5QwtnO0U5wgp6YN3aSMEFSmYyi8CNtpUfMm9sMRNSe0xZbMShhLOQmKWW" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Altar of Saturn, Rome.<br><br>The ancient altar of Saturn in the Forum, variously attributed to Ianus, the Pelasgians, Hercules, and Servius Tullius.<br><br> Sources locate the altar ‘at the bottom of the Clivus Capitolinus’ and ‘in front of the Senaculum’. The Senaculum was an open area in front of the Temple of Concord and Basilica Opimia in the late Republic, an area later occupied by Tiberius’ Temple of Augustan Concord. On the basis of these and other references, Coarelli has identified the cappellacio blocks behind the Rostra of Augustus, which Lanciani had associated with the Volcanal, as the remains of the altar of Saturn.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1548-F57C00</styleUrl>
