      <Placemark>
        <name>Iseum (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v7qSY1hAhhTOWFDN-YypqlWEXXgACbNopWl1z9gj-LJNSzWlTVI1e3BWiaQEBWdCVv_qepJqFmGhXVoIh4CdUo2eiEewLmKWiQuTbq2whJcOJ6VPgBFfxF1l7EMatPre4jFRpYXiKK7uoNmekQOsFu3xpG79k0TV5d56AGYqehGkGtsG7v_fsIO6ZV7Cm4caT_zxVIu88Og6-sh8nwvVC4PfBzbeHYtSHOZxzbwkyopT6CdX-U23tDGVAmh8uoJ12BjbahjZ3_WTaLMXit18f6x5WhMSVQ_bAvzUKMErjkTc-4_TvaEyXW-sF4tZlph6BvUouym4qLpMJND6VdVYpw6axX751P2FoW6K4UzqQR1mWO255ZJJAVReH_SDkJVuxajFye4L9Rf5NgqvRM9TrcBYbgieR6Z8OpOvL8o7Vk1fbF590xofDfs1zdCICP5Zem09p_274-XkgY0XelgzoxMK4HfafewO8QNKya54Cf4jzQe8haKxsSU5x70eOTT_45jpS-PRoCHDhJ-mpkl4yV7jNg_zlkub4YwTi-kQTLeQ2EBvaG5Xs6Jye1hBenTtoP8HvzoVjt_2VKijkg4GqnWIWPZxpLt_kL0cufaWoA74ZL_9tC6FvBRItIILG-c-STl2U-fHJdqhVphxpR0Sj-7SbBX3H4avbOg3fzl1xntwon1el7_qIE9tIedfAucnyNvFiUocHl9sA" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Temple of Isis, Rome.<br><br>The most important temple of Isis in Rome (and eventually, the Mediterranean) stood in the central Campus Martius, immediately E of the Porticus Meleagri, where it shared a sanctuary with an equally significant but separate Temple of Serapis. <br><br>The construction of this great Iseum is often, though without good reason, attributed to Caligula. It is more likely, however, that the temple was vowed by the Second Triumvirate in 43 BC.<br><br>This temple was completely destroyed by fire in 80 AD and subsequently rebuilt by Domitian. <br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gz_h1SgzjOkQzfRZ69HUj7_sUqw6mAhQlogpAbfMJdEo0SqyLOuYZA_WV2-7SwxxbVU-X_YAazJn4GYAfpuZ-yY5pC8cTN9WjSbd7UJ1XE9opjlEiini6HNRYQB-yyDcDCipnKGx9R6cooW22Y7Wa5v7rQwHhtStDaciKIsxxFcvePnII7Aejhl4P4Ji3C48WjDenQ-EgK_qg?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1548-FBC02D</styleUrl>
