      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Iseum (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Temple of Isis, Rome.<br><br>Imposing triportico with central water basin (piscina) found on a large terrace on the S slopes of the Oppian, in the probable position of the Iseum Metellinum and the sanctuary of Isis et Serapis of Regio III. This identification finds confirmation in the large number of Isiac statuary finds spread throughout this area. Two inscriptions found in the Via Labicana mention Isis. Numerous sculptures of Isis and other Egyptian deities have come to light near the Church of SS. Pietro e Marcellino, in Via Merulana–Via Buonarroti and Via dello Statuto to the N, and at scattered points on the Esquiline.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1548-FBC02D</styleUrl>
