      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Sacellum Murciae (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v4rnhShsuSwC2D0i6LxvtPdXsWAhUCru0i1-cWP6ZgHUO5Wl0d893Qd5aOdLH6FtqmkWMLWgZxnao6x4Hduk9cAUmtEeDnfkX1fJFS2ejjJZD0P6fs6MuQRlBm-MFhl276RBZDrBM7G0XtLWUJxdfgRUfP3aaCAX9Ef2sDz2RjzLAFYVbnkKMPliyoUcHWgJBiZsNgPWAzHdQ0QXU0hWG8kHiljET96bwSJO_fxH6ZhTqFhbZ6khDUn4jlahN5INrCnRinDIW5qndBjPusNImT9sPAdv3SG0pSjFX5vYqXKhY_bmdD6IwU4By-lnwVow1ic6V2jA0EVLa6SWI1w00yIU2gVE-OuGN4_uZddV-OQoOm4LNPOwRufOISrYLSlZzaBLMRELzFFB1S4VjEBgecr4YfVH1Pne2MwZ5aiHJMkLgHORJTQwQQFGhBTfU0B5oiEoZ9NL4awTHaeMzZyejdTm0Ti8zDlrLLYzbiY71zsg75iD0Hi6MHFagng-qAiffU94tWdTKgZxZTsy9jb-8PkZvTxI4Bvq8YWzc8NPgzW4E9fyGP931izJN6yPumoLnlCZy37e75-U5wk_EsWIi_7-7p-tLNhC483yFED2ookLGrxTqHisfjy585fwnZHO6nIcKr68j0B5AdKeHNinDvFnW8Vh1UBXEgYqKR_OAn_K27Lwj5TfS2PqOrZCWKIiM8NCHrrvFu_5A" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Shrine to Murcia, Rome.<br><br>The shrine of the archaic divinity Murcia stood within the track of the Circus Maximus near the first turning post (the SE meta) on the Aventine side.<br><br> Varro relates that the small shrine was once surrounded by a grove, but this had been reduced to a single myrtle tree, a vestigium, by the Augustan era. In late antiquity the valley was called the vallis Murcia after the goddess, but perhaps only after her shrine had been substantially enlarged.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1548-795548</styleUrl>
