      <Placemark>
        <name>Sacellum Pudicitiae Plebeiae (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Shrine to Pudicitia Plebeia, Rome.<br><br>Shrine to Pudicitia Plebeia, founded in 296 BC by the patrician matron Verginia in part of her residence on the Vicus Longus along the SE slope of the Quirinal. <br><br>While Livy records that the cult fell into oblivion after worship was taken up by women of questionable character, Festus writes as though the cult was still active in his day; thus it may well have had a presence in Augustan Rome.]]></description>
