      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Aesculapii (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v4s9PmKeo9L8xwDjv49Pwrw6m0Ycjy7NXH9sH5ryfzIm-qVh9mHsS1M4wn2lm5TgHoD5gYQL2dK64hh_EBMALMinDJnSSVjTfhpeDD6zEq97mx1OMszzgQLugacJ7q2QD1teXsUNMPeQr018IP2k7ta1-zj9gX1jOQ6CaeIJNSMxk5xlbbAGXv1eY0ZaD0TYoqRgnUxKXymOlkbvjGVJJUQBY1GprsheJ3tsvVUfngNZDY6nvKx0i2fKhzqDH99g1ShG1iPEVvcaQ5wbUsSVaEF0t483To_W-_Or-lUP7mmVLN83867gSyx1hWDoxl-1b85-oelMFdchurjCIQYm9vC23WnH8coLuLh1NhbdQ5BRlN2Dk6d_43A1btUobg-SPNNte9MGZ5INihrUo1SAD76sCVtVUwdaCHmiP7a3jMXopUii1qDmbcUNiKaZD7wVCD5emIo2BE-BgAsiyflJMxhwBaHpLaypZYEKljQkcMhC3fTq24J6B315lGwJZTms8rO9JqBZFRoGXmnbyyEp4Nw6VKalJ7VJYFhSc_qmsvLXNpbD73y48HoiCkjpGW-hobCrhmVs5W1fMQ08bSLKM9c0VTbfJq5fzqY2xNAGqKFofnV-aVQ2RS6EIy2nN6Ac4fImqYzKRHLajF5RrkdutT0k_WrFdIe-QIRpi4JGbVPg46GJUL0lmv5phRoSnTCFtQXslnsUDGJ" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Temple of Aesculapius, Rome.<br><br>The Temple to Aesculapius (Greek Asclepius), built on the Tiber island in 293 BC after a serious plague occasioned the introduction of the cult to Rome.<br><br> From this time on, the Insula Tiberina acted as a place of refuge and of healing in the Republican city. Both literary and epigraphic evidence suggests that the temple, along with the entire island, underwent a major reconstruction and monumentalization around the mid-1st c. BC.<br><br>The Temple of Aesculapius is believed to have stood on the SE end of the island, probably under the Church of S. Bartolomeo. Although the temple is archaeologically unknown, the mid-1st c. BC travertine and tufa revetment at the S tip of the island imitating a trireme prow and its reliefs (head of Aesculapius and a staff entwined with a serpent), as well as the terracotta votive offerings from the head of the Pons Fabricius, strongly support this location. It seems likely that a small-scale temple stood at the very S end, directly above the prow. <br><br>The Severan Marble Plan suggests that the small precinct was composed of a courtyard enclosed with a series of rooms.<br><br><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v6hRx3VP0llhwBdt3ALpepxgOFQMMwom4fUtnMoSulP74leFkjxeW57NZ7bqyqRf4vLJpZfDg8kOH1OlPq6ofrcmyE1NK28yRKKN-fX8HuSJ_7mAYoIn-IR8xALBdlc_ouESj_DVPBEYVmcpi-0rt4PDFoG7O6YoMshKUGHuQHSM9IpA_zLusF8mlhh1zEjhWpeE8RpTk74e86xEzMhphZkBD0Ncdd9s4TfhIjebZangxvwTX9_OoWFgnV2iuwf5pi-_sU2vMIMPjffK_xAKmFA68qCg6iNakZByecj2YzNCUByvEavsBVPqSQWMMcEyQ2B7fHhR31jbrOxKV2JOQC0POBvGmgr0vc4VL5pXw0w95oFKw4n6dMHpBiXp4GhLpL_GHFVQYN2r47Wfu5563HJP2deTpamNVoZ5DOZsxw7bEnwkrVPwusdydou_LLrte5BcDMN-nCc43WveW3afghOz9FrTf7xkum7HW2uPHGzaUiw5KrdZ8jrJERV5xG8GgN7pHauwNB9T_LyEM_sQsT5eA8_c-KOrMBMQSJf304qYdxtbmfRG7ejdAnM3GimxQ_g0LjyWsaXWWRmvxbNWNkZXZdulniMQ_hC3loi6RZVq7a3i369TrFQaKWJTNEGlNQRuqa82pD0DCPAyG-JiWE9oIXxfpASNDKUmyaraOZaDvUG3McFlrNupEjv6LeqAKaXJP93vb49" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v5Inq47GL_YR2eEmohbqSgh2oAE0rirHA1rJE3zzNSC5WBVZYQHKRUqez_u7VbkSFSqBkJP_-pqhMSL26FW1uxecodQNzAzdk8DHOw50efPc62p7whtl6Wqz7SgMBWvHlzAau2XOddnGSiLjyLo8Erej_orAKfMf-oaIzPixYFQVbt1n6KCgrGIQFdtEWO-0gaWvB3sP-5RsJeNozMJewfdx_BZEbqZbn7C8Ts4kgSEszfdpgB6ZpCRpmuspqce5dWIK3vN9eKSjQ1fyxT7W8nRFKp0XFoM2OpGChnc1PCc31aJ1_as7H1ovJpLV49BR3q-UQVFar4Xf0WEyvtW-0z2j66Qzw1UkEuosQA9Bt3kInBxcxq-orrN-a3c-nVioojdA_xFvR79A0tdS9dLOlGMEsdDWbWq8lxG3VqAbQghJu7VQo5NlNVcr2HlpWkLuopywaT-Zv9hV_zCwzuZ67G2wKaqdupNnA8xBdyWnouTO53yeoLuTp9C9JtPaA5w641T0yyl1M_9LaqSFUHPMXwVyro5h_lwGDT3LUvh0FML-3BxCZkTdDL_LoDCL63La997UlZZiPvYA7aqgMllLc1q75ab9DgpPn4hjWFXscbxD4dR-4L633feCWewd_VtQIdq_JSvqCsN_dGiBvRR62L66gn7oIWgw1sk9asAoAoeg1SJ-9S_J-q-OIxVZ1ZcBeCx7A7dNUAFTQ" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
