      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Apollonis Medici (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v7C5tuJ9actqYnIwsCkPpEg7i_V-Ay7dQXJwP670fwMuw1zabeUGmQ_2TOOLA__rSJ3u7DnRHoefESrFt9kJ8aKl5eRtbhGAL2GXdz0RLbexJeIPsc3Ywh9DiQEN0J6Mt9O7jPEjUyAY7ay8hlVSTSRyBhfDX7f05NYbyt6jVocjjBta5jcaGIWaeZ_nlujzBTroSFIuhJVr70NWNspL8TbUDPedupoCr5Eq4tf3LkIHz2o3m5m1mec2ZW505Rm5dihWlfm9AnTfgmi-o_HVrRUg4SPaYnOYUVK581AinevIJGSTUlk6aY2I2-gOFhGm6PpyyxBIO9_sdpSLQ5tw_Uw8Ukkbz-t9wKtjN77TBiC5uco90YoKQNDeRHBXIj6ojsHki6-6Xzjpmnko3UcFiVcSDXwR7B3r-SNuclkMU71WbUu32tkej_Z1plsM3AmtPCaaMC_UWE1cLPcDMjdsfgNTLbquk7GF3hzZtUS_QwJUtTndp3CqBpDR4blN5SLuLm-ghqttyUh6x84QvyE3pzfNAhQPtrAaC_iozh3YQno28wbiJotjvcmY0o2gAPZSAA3nIiC7qjTGM52_yu-EDcCHLFQ-vG1Mt33wnWVWRZ4M12K3YcZqn5DemjYLHAxXetRFUvzZMfQIc7gTAKvXOK5ANcNx_TAph4qItTGx5Yz1bfbumsJm5ILFHXW7I5jqsfEtYLLNq-X_w" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Temple of Apollo Medicus, Rome.<br><br>The Temple of Apollo, specifically of Apollo Medicus, was situated outside the Servian Wall ‘between the Forum Holitorium and the Circus Flaminius’. It was ‘by the Theater of Marcellus’.<br><br> Lavishly rebuilt in the Augustan period by C. Sosius (cos. 32 BC), thus also known as Apollo Sosianus, the temple was one of the most richly-decorated in Rome.<br><br>The cult of Apollo Medicus had long been an architectural presence on the site, since in 433-431 BC it was vowed and dedicated by the consul C. Iulius following a plague. It has been proposed that in the early 2nd c. BC the temple was substantially rebuilt in relation to the construction of a new theatre in the area in 179 BC. This tetrastyle-diastyle Temple of Apollo was excavated in part below the Augustan phase of the temple.<br><br>Well-preserved remains document, indisputably, the complete rebuilding of the temple by C. Sosius following a new design, probably after his victory in Judea in 34 BC. The pictorial narratives of the internal frieze suggest that Augustus may have been responsible for the completion of the project, presumably after his triumphs in 29 BC; otherwise C. Sosius must have re-oriented his ideology for this narrative program.<br><br><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v72EntdDbtjqvR8yFD3VFk0MLi90dqQghUNplfilhkoKbtz7j2oHRsR_mQEG5bTjr5IXfCxyONCUFqzq0-YHZ0N3mqC9DdWUqdzx7XC59duoRlD0vL7DBqPHJ_eaOC6xGdg99XaygVyp08z0805rzmoIQA9saCO0X-CDI86O60Dau3XJvlT02wKurr6-Qu8q-7YTvEtiUWMTyQCq054cPf6AXNSTq1VqpQ0mWM6tT2lnwu4PnlQLfsCQYIcSQ5Rzd78JZtlJqUPHJPp_snaR0eqQLeNeZIFtvwLdZFxcC_gLN9Y1OPwv-OxxyowxOaKpj9oH_qSFZlOmiMfT8d3pvPD0HQxo-ER0zpYw4KGoQFP7yhbG4oHdP5cjuV3PJ2L3WFsKk3dsc1HbZh0Hz_dGLkIhzPNalpRkNtDw1Kclqi1PrT-6x6gFKPmdu_jw53M7Tu9Ekh3-nCdEryhzPV0zFcYdRgNThQNqHFcQEyEyvWc4fTUL72yX32h9SPmFJZVsuPnYB9c3-hZZlf6z4MhfR4VKnd7jjiZFURUetkHYPpBVxKCnjnufKqqf-xonLKlp1GHP9dlKMSXN7tC7W1s6bJbRT8WKmxj9aj9flu62v_gbl50wfMuIddsJlu5_S4kA4gZv4x5puGd9M-XCqiHQXW-9D1TcMZ3wr7sUuCX8VnO9d6SGjrtzAyM6g1kul9HzCMKgkOebPGSpA" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v6nIUKjX_cNMC3I1nzHukzmDxKbecFflZWOtpz4DA10qwBo4W3NJQcTG4NkasPWrZxFXM6a0It7ZdQd4oxRKeNk64wrd5kbK2CZD0fB-OTr3Ayd89LPRE05Ar95bzj0flnJDGSfCumcY4fiq3aTs7iriSSwTysSu0UtB1JkCG9B3vSRCEqNq5AEAMm5sZtXMcytFwWHk_TzGIQAOiyCwYjJnbTCfQREVNUlml6DhvYg0kRzDqVjqlyB9K4HE-DBxqaKuXsy-xuzbXLdds-jBi98rjRRosADnDALKZ6-f4OWNXTK8ftnN32OBvuwpaRPnjb_NzPkYSN03BXGGK4W4eIqcTOqhuEAW7kzTYmrqmttQj4zr37XdXoeMKZYBluvk3nCiYyen5rgOpi60GyKIbmjt0_i1cTniGEKQerlt5jEXtFgLL0U7wE_UCwRaT4c_czSUVk4ETFvqxcXmG74rwiZVojTONtkEocJOwRWSV_do3TagyOJsfrEPp3ancfr5Y9S7HS2En7xwwImf3U3HAy1cRMFM3o3Qt9JRcEewY9Q4sFkd6qa3gnWldb6mJxJgIR_Ic04299ALve1IXsbmBAtV_3U9T19oIUOKLbU5nOOl6o7IMf6OpMVwILJWB4qgF4scRDiD2MICA_hSlE8Du2cnZCoxD2jgWsvn4cKmnRmg6KGGQ8W2fvGKIrZDgavOC4OkUQoWstv" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
