      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Castoris et Pollucis (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v5O2JXxdhgF1fqztglDd5SK5UaXSx9WKqTr4CyPFLd_wRoOmZxq16XeVOMEo07SzOYFnBVscQAvZ8TUR9hfou-oBKuJm9mUS__kOWIgXGDCfZFGD3hkQJ_nzOXf8_Jpd2IPLSjoku23OCTDj7poPKlQ9vp4LhxRK0LwjMPI6fD2q22CSmsuQ7GLK6G2m9m3PpZlhDuxtqEFy5myaJyDj6hHCsENv2FUtaFN6FCJKq9GZLtcOsePirUYgJSQ_RUqJ0-0r3y_1WgSSZDA-N1nxreb4dH3kfMR3Cq6Ker1unaT3ILRgkchRcFbVIZMDri8RpsVti2vOEYzOmkTCvr8nVKRIvzyVRPP5x3EocojeO6QU5AqUPfvXoj2aMIT_4CUhAab9hzRxic0LfL_h_iecPs_pFHQ8fll8SY3iBjOf2aEDxlNaWCn7yDtlGsRKCV9oMSeqAKgTFgM2eANVC_o0FtgtzVyRuYnb0upEa_H7oSU_OlWohLViHa7EtP4Xl1XYoRaeF9JzYLA7HQFXjZSeWa9enWgHP9mDhsFfl_AZXbInAMTTqsZvlW4kbqUddvjREeiXKRGabyKNB_k_3MpQzOcoDMt12NKy_8oY2UgcSLgXCFpMICHywERylBmZlbJOuyjVlVpyYumHGEflE5srBYZous5ReVXqTBSsScsfTDqQ0yHT2mpJ-gv5_wBx32TTfbvCPOYvoAKaQ" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Temple of Castor & Pollux, Rome.<br><br>Tetrastyle, prostyle temple along the SW side of the Circus Flaminius dedicated to Castor and Pollux, characterized by an unusual transverse cella, similar to the Tiberian Temple of Concordia Augusta or the Temple of Veiovis. <br><br>The limited space available for the construction of the temple between the Circus Flaminius and the Tiber may have dictated this plan, though it should be noted that no archaeological evidence of contemporaneous structures on the W side of the Circus Flaminius has been uncovered.<br><br>Only three literary sources mention the structure: Vitruvius, the calendars (fasti), and Plutarch, who mentions that a Caecilius Metellus decorated the Temple of the Dioscuri with statues and images; this person may have also donated the temple itself. Since the name of this temple is present in the fasti Amiternini and Antiati, both written before the Caesarian change of the calendar in 46 BC, that year should be taken as terminus ante quem. Therefore, Plutarch’s Metellus must be identified with Q. Caecilius Metellus Pius who triumphed in Spain in 71 BC and built the temple using war booty (ex manubiis) soon after.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1548-795548</styleUrl>
