      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Concordiae Augustae (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v5w-cWdKyUCWSZ3AH9pGkFguJvwbLcLpLiwXaefrfOK06eRuvLp6ch5Bjc6XU1Y8xHee7dwpjYWQPsbsG_WyvhJLen-_IKmF9Qoco4oZ5CLT7tR8mY2dg0Pej9OOmuI9JuqHksAvl17oqpQhjX7eOiuyMNBD0OB6zg29QbngYLFScF88BuoGGtv57aZiqL3zpmniaix_v2ZLzbWI0XfFr52Mnpxb8JQ97PveKldpTp3dqG2rHNHsa85PAdtp5xdLAZN6_QWS02Ckxwq92zL-pLyW4eFuLZhdxfZZ3OrWJ7yHskLmh_DvrEAya5VqV6izZG-jBXz45Xg3JH1qiRbgc87ecKH3sY5wu1QL3SnMVurXGJu4o4T_BVlELXQA2ZrL-Dg3ETKoULr5_cxnIkMb3Ddj9SM9_B4eXBIaNKooiCZDvt_gpI479kfmMOiaFtoCXU6i9qR2tOJegaGYZqzo1kFG59zJPOfoVJ761JEZB_uO4v3jGcpPMBWuY-ROwIARshgwf0XX74PSJDDpNjBbICbYlooWqul2W7UAykmV_uAfw0XDVkOpUmb582lS_CPgbJQtNqXABRsdDawrAW4geoegoIDGnskJNDPB1Vamc1gggayz7WyHtweK0AfbKeB9ReygIJoVF48NWxWXkOU8IpQrkheTOWLUNqykqwLAFUoRXdxMTanQlWrhIVzOznE4ybCvH0huP6KpA" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Temple of Concordia Augusta, Rome.<br><br>The Temple of Augustan Concord at the foot of the Capitolium overlooking the Forum. <br><br>According to Roman tradition, the Temple of Concord was originally vowed by Camillus during patrician-plebeian struggles in 367 BC. Although the people voted to build the temple on behalf of Camillus, it is unclear whether this temple was ever built, though recent excavations have uncovered 4th c. BC remains on the site.<br><br> A temple to Concordia was definitely built by L. Opimius in 121 BC following the death of C. Gracchus, but this temple burned, perhaps in 9 BC. Tiberius vowed to restore the temple in 7 BC and the rebuilt temple, now to Augustan Concord, was dedicated in the names of Tiberius and his dead brother Drusus.<br><br>The visible remains of the temple are from the Augustan phase. The cella, which abuts the Tabularium, has a transverse axis, an unusual design that maximizes the available space. The new temple probably covered the Volcanal, an altar to Vulcan said to have been erected by Titus Tatius. The NE façade of the pronaos and the NE half of the cella, now underneath the adjacent staircase ascending the Capitolium, are restored on the principle of symmetry.<br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gwcknsg_XRGr1sFRSXFjofaOhFNJkU-uRhw8SZJiGOJJPKLxMU_txJbQNrLJfgUZlRm0JHED-RKe0oqtNgXByPv0sjUyfQhqMgJkH4111znyI_jUEhCy4QhHClgVDHrHFDlWD_xc1bYVVkCkgyPHrK9t2AVagqev_y72bk2z7iUWqVGhS6j0NBwFnc3rIz1MZgKExWEEMXilgk?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1548-795548</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v5w-cWdKyUCWSZ3AH9pGkFguJvwbLcLpLiwXaefrfOK06eRuvLp6ch5Bjc6XU1Y8xHee7dwpjYWQPsbsG_WyvhJLen-_IKmF9Qoco4oZ5CLT7tR8mY2dg0Pej9OOmuI9JuqHksAvl17oqpQhjX7eOiuyMNBD0OB6zg29QbngYLFScF88BuoGGtv57aZiqL3zpmniaix_v2ZLzbWI0XfFr52Mnpxb8JQ97PveKldpTp3dqG2rHNHsa85PAdtp5xdLAZN6_QWS02Ckxwq92zL-pLyW4eFuLZhdxfZZ3OrWJ7yHskLmh_DvrEAya5VqV6izZG-jBXz45Xg3JH1qiRbgc87ecKH3sY5wu1QL3SnMVurXGJu4o4T_BVlELXQA2ZrL-Dg3ETKoULr5_cxnIkMb3Ddj9SM9_B4eXBIaNKooiCZDvt_gpI479kfmMOiaFtoCXU6i9qR2tOJegaGYZqzo1kFG59zJPOfoVJ761JEZB_uO4v3jGcpPMBWuY-ROwIARshgwf0XX74PSJDDpNjBbICbYlooWqul2W7UAykmV_uAfw0XDVkOpUmb582lS_CPgbJQtNqXABRsdDawrAW4geoegoIDGnskJNDPB1Vamc1gggayz7WyHtweK0AfbKeB9ReygIJoVF48NWxWXkOU8IpQrkheTOWLUNqykqwLAFUoRXdxMTanQlWrhIVzOznE4ybCvH0huP6KpA https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gwcknsg_XRGr1sFRSXFjofaOhFNJkU-uRhw8SZJiGOJJPKLxMU_txJbQNrLJfgUZlRm0JHED-RKe0oqtNgXByPv0sjUyfQhqMgJkH4111znyI_jUEhCy4QhHClgVDHrHFDlWD_xc1bYVVkCkgyPHrK9t2AVagqev_y72bk2z7iUWqVGhS6j0NBwFnc3rIz1MZgKExWEEMXilgk?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
