      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Fauni (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v64zOnHRDG0zbARFup21Tm2OS3uKDnr4SFg30MVzB0tblviVVGyVbtrGwqjyUuFIEjDyZMhTqTDU-85-hBBiXUcecTcPjfe6Y1nuj0l2a8aBVPmfBiYYK7BFdhFrSQXVCwpgFhbpN-Jtfk9r24lKb-Q7sCvWfQox6-gGdXT__FENVPJoUwigfOiNVt4ev-LY6XwyrAvtsiZ_dFzZqIdbDDXMb4CYdmvd5fNFO1eboFJFVS-BGICKhetIDJvivwiA08dR6qtqfxOV2deeyoSvCxYdzoexh86t_09QNuQO4n12rXu7QWT3-gajy99FChN_0s4bp0Kfur_r30E2qUTRuOl6tzMN6TeGzoCNK-3EoO3mzttCKKwNKoyujGF8eM8fug7MscLiPTXWwWSvtwpmrG1XBG1OeyFTfJHN2W9MW5y-a-EyfoD3AKhj89-9H1KLQRO3_5ES8hbzvwO1vH-4SE7CQvQsuhXPLIzHXpZMqBYxaxFEE5YYFxRfLcKt3uijB_IU1iQ-DNO7DcDvRCeH3pCFxMU6OMSOsMmKQndCwWfK9AV6ioflab3gRggPfFR5ucAX1Xv3NEw821pgkExIooASgB9qJ16_4bYH8qJM5aKkkJ7lbSqYWdxmcHZChK9TchYYld8SGBqJ-5KlPu9BzoSUbxmZVlklnNuLt-W2NhpYeDx3WY0EDVjSQslBjS30Kv7xKVbti8b" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Temple of Faunus, Rome.<br><br>A temple was dedicated to Faunus, an ancient Latin god of the forest and its prophetic voices, in 196 BC at the N end of the Tiber island. <br><br>It was vowed by the tribuni plebis, Cn. Domitius Ahenobarbus and C. Scribonius Curio, and dedicated by the praetor urbanus of the time. Vitruvius mentions the building as an example of the tetrastyle, prostyle temple. ]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1548-795548</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
