      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Febris (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Temple of Febris, Rome.<br><br>A minor sanctuary dedicated to Febris on the Quirinal, situated at the highest point of the Vicus Longus.<br><br> Its date, form, size and exact location are unknown, and no archaeological remains are associated with it.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1548-795548</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            12.497084,41.905763,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Felicitatis (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Temple of Felicitas, Rome.<br><br>A Temple of Felicitas in the NW corner of the Forum, planned by Caesar and built by M. Aemilius Lepidus in 44 BC. <br><br>According to Dio, the temple was erected on the site of the old Curia Hostilia as the formal justification for the Curia’s demolition. Although it is often assumed that this temple was itself destroyed soon after its erection, there is no evidence for its destruction before or during the Augustan period, and monumental remains discovered under the Church of SS. Luca e Martina adjacent to the Forum Iulium are now thought to belong to this structure.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1548-795548</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            12.48454,41.892497,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Feroniae (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v5ygblxQ-2QE0mi_OpJWmVdW-YnsWgWi8j0b9-5BY5_os1k176rg33rRu_AtwQLChX9D0CBJs0L_ZlQ7wA6e3e7dJXUYJSAFTk767T9tGcH2du_qGi7bUo1vYZfgIlZcxxv2DTvxqwtqbM1_72kiZA6sdQJ3Y-ma_mVtnL0Bkm5xwzSQZUK0hTso2_3Ugyjev86Sdp1ucIziMKWOLSMBWPItzP18nOoVN8uLqosIKTzQ55-tPxwYzPQ2jX0S6aEbZzrkmcmOiIPGc4AjMoQdMEKunAQGGmSsbBzrFjVk98JMtH-s_T-YMZfyBQjFG43SmtqjlgMMyCElEMiaU3RydJugJVzDlEBA_xXchU85oovKl4nnBeRhOhOvJrvngiHu-FiSmQq2ecqJWlCKJIXbDQCjef6VrjrSuhtRpV1gfai0m9BtqQYbk2vgryO2RmGi1iqMALQRX0H2UKNweL_L4SWJiTIzcKj-EVDtw9iMCyVkd8QeUB3vnorH5ciX4Qp11YS1flzcXcLWyGvL40O5ypXYArxZr36mHv2U_Z5EEzuNTianDZy3C2uWrtFC4ejns1vN3jl64RNz7JvOqwDDfhNCD06bTSws-xr0jMzKCog8AYAxfZqB24bcwRb7ksK6nEnyUdfYODWrvMZOcTl5xamI6qR55GjHdUbQraNACTgfg-f0kQ9H76U_l-mABisQBzpCVgoSqwv" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Temple of Feronia, Rome.<br><br>One of the four known temples in the sacral area near Largo Argentina, Temple C was perhaps the oldest, originally built in the first half of the 3rd c. BC concurrently with, or slightly earlier than, Temple A. <br><br>The temple was prostyle, tetrastyle sine postico, with widely-spaced façade columns perhaps of the Tuscan order. The massive tufa podium, with heavy moldings typical of the early 3rd c. BC, still stands, though the visible remains of the cella floor and superstructure are Domitianic in date.<br><br>Before the mid-2nd c. BC, a new altar built on a large platform in front of the temple, and inscribed A. POSTVMIVS A. F. A. N. ALBINVS DVOVIR LEGE PLAETORIA REFICIVNDAM COERAVIT, replacing the original. The altar was still a prominent feature in the Augustan era, for even though the installation of the first tufa pavement engulfed the platform, care was taken to leave the altar exposed; it was finally buried by a second pavement dating to 80 AD.<br><br><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v45G4HCo2uBk7AJx0EnOPdiNnSIbzo6vKv5J4vFnFFhKfef2paEA1mTUpwUHPbgb5cIxHUdVm1sfT-kS6sZxz1XVV4tfLOuRVGJ0O--2KPBgFY5YdEyd8-PH_gnObxckj0yD6ncn3FzdYgEOwNx4U6dJtsMO-GUuEyGe16Z3ZfOJT_d9FFEx2N1bdzKnDy5n3xczucdAz7Q0NOWXOVPeSpbEGKxohyuHIQq5HDJF7gvwF2xvSM3kuRTVGGhLsfimom6-r6pRF2hIf1D-czd8wBAGqLouDN2vHkC4cd9hM_PLwNMsxaL-nt3S1IUvH-pyjsiL4lUICt8Y-_rSQuRA_T_0l7-kQYkYBYmsl8CdRHOHP2u6W9_F3UwnylV5sivrCuxM7gcacWdwBCJSrt_tD21Mmb91MbyvREyWW3VJFq7jOCFcfeTJoELgzqzN7qIFRWHYqQQqyIG7kSDWxRuxJRDqNve0vrxbIrmWtAi7lTOE-3dA1lK6rKm1NGVeaKLMmTgw4oJaPVpSNssfv_ke9DiwPUmw1MXpVKRnqxwJtBMKlHuCBZSSoEr3KiAvDg3g4-40y_klLN6Tj2qtvTX-3UibI_Q05jVdz-Nfr5r15KMwGAtAnZ9waMXixnuOzdKOd9J2CyPBJA0Z1IjK8dwa-U4Uda6J1a3Iab4_8AAiVh_px_w305Cmn_dmS-GsW5fH_QVsW9S3arttg" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
