      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Fortunae Primigeniae (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Temple of Fortuna Primigenia, Rome.<br><br>A trio of Republican temples dedicated to Fortuna and known as the Tres Fortunae was located near the Porta Collina on the Quirinal.<br><br> One was dedicated to Fortuna Primigenia in 194 BC by Q. Marcius Ralla to fulfill a vow made 10 years earlier by P. Sempronius Tuditanus. <br><br>Ovid records a second temple, this dedicated to Fortuna Publica; Fortuna Publica Citerior may have been the full name of this temple which the fasti Praenestini locate on the Quirinal. <br><br>A third temple honoured Fortuna Publica Populi Romani Quiritium, which the calendars also locate IN COLLE QVIRINALI.<br><br>Thus, three temples of Fortuna are known to have been located on the collis Quirinalis near the Porta Collina.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1548-E65100</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            12.49792,41.907624,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Fortunae Publicae Citerioris (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Temple of Fortuna Publica Citerior, Rome.<br><br>A trio of Republican temples dedicated to Fortuna and known as the Tres Fortunae was located near the Porta Collina on the Quirinal.<br><br>One was dedicated to Fortuna Primigenia in 194 BC by Q. Marcius Ralla to fulfill a vow made 10 years earlier by P. Sempronius Tuditanus.<br><br>Ovid records a second temple, this dedicated to Fortuna Publica; Fortuna Publica Citerior may have been the full name of this temple which the fasti Praenestini locate on the Quirinal.<br><br>A third temple honoured Fortuna Publica Populi Romani Quiritium, which the calendars also locate IN COLLE QVIRINALI.<br><br>Thus, three temples of Fortuna are known to have been located on the collis Quirinalis near the Porta Collina.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1548-E65100</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            12.497764,41.907532,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Fortunae Publicae Populorum Romanorum Quiritium (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Temple of Fortuna Publica Populi Romani Quiritium, Rome.<br><br>A trio of Republican temples dedicated to Fortuna and known as the Tres Fortunae was located near the Porta Collina on the Quirinal.<br><br>One was dedicated to Fortuna Primigenia in 194 BC by Q. Marcius Ralla to fulfill a vow made 10 years earlier by P. Sempronius Tuditanus.<br><br>Ovid records a second temple, this dedicated to Fortuna Publica; Fortuna Publica Citerior may have been the full name of this temple which the fasti Praenestini locate on the Quirinal.<br><br>A third temple honoured Fortuna Publica Populi Romani Quiritium, which the calendars also locate IN COLLE QVIRINALI.<br><br>Thus, three temples of Fortuna are known to have been located on the collis Quirinalis near the Porta Collina.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1548-E65100</styleUrl>
