      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Herculis Primigenii (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Temple of Hercules Primigenius, Rome.<br><br>Sanctuary of Hercules Primigenius, located outside the Servian Wall, along the Via Salaria.<br><br> Hannibal camped here in 211 BC. <br><br>Though no archaeological evidence survives, the location of this cult site can safely be inferred from the shrine of Hercules Primigenius, known from Augustan and Julio-Claudian funerary inscriptions and a marble cippus inscribed to Hercules Primigenius, found in the area of Piazza Fiume.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1548-4E342E</styleUrl>
