      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Iovis Optimi Maximi Capitolini (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v5qeG1lfN3eEFq0--ewKCeQyiTDru1yi5ne8GAJ8iFeewlDNxv7zDITI0p5H8QqMGExc5aSRyEG0g4yc9VrabmM5jPnDr-BdDnvX53lDUPrqcFMP5Q2DfXDvgG-4874maDn7rH8bcqRu5kEl2WdI5Cj6MjO1CuJtNbeCzN4A8aYG7L7ES0HJ8i9l5rlYdE8dBpHFk4q2-ruAWhapbrmQhYuni7SVZ-5jIQTAyd1Q4KKT8dlOes3uL4p6O54PS3vdtV5cKXt0AOTMynmFvT5uBha5pHs1rKwdMbsMZN2p7Vm73ik8EKjyloLAYkKRHULRg83mp_H5UWZYfBuqObZ_HN6aXdm1-PAJGW8ylB_7j-X41y8by3o0cgUVM_s1n2JtWAufdhQcYoLg22WsWalYnix32hzAm9WNvvE7L0RTWM-nEUd2OMRz5QfdjPHIO0iJ3O7pU8oCu86CQsn23H3EkYVUBEgb38njhAMP9RmqnAzIFywerVoKSoGD9PTLfjflY0LMYzKGP4BK8gnXnDFjq2xyE33ahZoNzas6SFd97nyTCEw7sBxWXGrjjuYpAH0nl_tAD1gZe84Fa6SVyxRqUzDyccoSyMRGpg101dTKt_-W0peKiCxKnJou6yBPOdDKY-VzTZR17zYTmnQGAtQT2r-CHDo2d2iJcH1DZBQA8SQ0jePz5r1lxBetqpNRKXdJjIRPahsTsF8" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Temple of Jupiter Optimus Maximus Capitolinus, Rome.<br><br>The Temple of Iuppiter Optimus Maximus has been identified, since 1683, with the foundations under Palazzo Caffarelli in the Area Capitolina. <br><br>Originally dating from the Archaic period, this huge temple was arguably the most important and revered sacred building in Rome. It was dedicated to the Capitoline Triad: Iuppiter Optimus Maximus, Iuno Regina, and Minerva, and incorporated preexisting shrines to Terminus, Iuventas, and Mars.<br><br> Excavations undertaken since 1865 have revealed enough to reconstruct a rectangular podium c. 62 x 53 m in area and 3.6 m high. North of the rear side of the podium is a parallel foundation which was part of the temenos wall of the Area Capitolina, not part of the temple. <br><br>Several construction phases are visible: a layer of capellaccio tufa blocks (H. c. 30-32 cm) set into the bedrock, 5 layers of the same tufa (H. c. 40 cm) set back slightly from the course below and, on top, a layer of concrete. However, there are fewer distinct construction phases than known restorations, and the dating of these levels is disputed. <br><br>The Archaic temple burned in 83 BC. The new temple was started by L. Cornelius Sulla and dedicated by Q. Lutatius Catulus in 69 BC. It was subsequently damaged by lightning on a number of occasions and restored by Augustus at great expense, perhaps after a fire in 9 BC. It is fairly certain from the existing podium remains that the Augustan temple as well as its antecedents and successors all stood on the same foundations. Above the level of the podium, the Temple of Iuppiter Optimus Maximus is generally restored in the Tuscan order, with three narrow cellae set behind a deep porch supported by three rows of 6 columns in a peripteros sine postico arrangement. In addition, there must have been a flight of steps in front of the façade, yet nothing survives of these steps in the archaeological record.<br><br><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v634UuaqjbV2cmdCTb2-Kl3toa2TMd8XuJ5PDYC_sDv8emcjiqjQJXwgGLIZ-2xscLAkuiIZCw_Tic26mLhwJrpODZwmTQtsOVwhFAWAo97fdRsbVWjrmjdZy_06G5g41BBLhImty03INSKHdIbKaaMtMkIdWtRi0Ps_eJKzFFYjUUiqSkpkiHldJ6QoYj9suIb3kXRL3f05QllLy6mdHyuwEGz8FWGTC6b_dojUoliKIUUxMcmEGi-rKoIgjdDpdB0XAS9zfcA2LM0EXf9rgVBZH_AcalkZE-ePE21EJUGUz1t5QpKj-sOAf_9ULdE5KxFvqT4XnbNUMA5GeiSVIuAWZo-SAswfsoRU6bW73dDEd_-dUgAcJzev9OrEGRL1YETyewCvf7D1vrvGDbnvcF2_WlDVcpKjdCz-bzuProXUCSU3cpOakJYPn7ucfqiVTv_rdrN4JTinrzKdq1DLNthfO-YF0F6P4Q28QsTZONyJ_uxg120oy7Cn35716TywhLyV8u2897QHFRx6RJ8587s0kvlr4_zFFupScb_IyXB23RsTe6O_iChTCxViK_L5yHl_zbepA0aOzE6_Y-ZLxe3xZD4Y8DJe45FIlkdIsYjf6imsxmmGr3XIuAx-9jtFb95tnU2RzNhfaTJVWEHdVXR9WjHWotrMHentz0TbDjaTVK3HpUOUSqEB3ijoDeN7o-K-vzvlB2gvg" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v6LuYPFtpZKZJrbuU86dhfS08tYEc-wyVB6wqPkUNd3nV0o6w6dDZ2xHPeb7nf-0-YPJuCHN7r969Txm5XHtsiGZTGUcnPxOGt0hLvROsvVeJueWtuw601KoRv5u0yDA57BLSFV0QArOay0iAoJp5CSuFRZwOv816szSz84dX9Mein0rUF19v8H6CuyglJWB_fH51CvTRohXECXFdvHmm7MPi0ialPBVBgbrkiTE1bgW_6lW0hIFlU6hNh0xA4aKYpdaIu7ca7HHO__tuHtgC3EXDntKpO8cc3xQDY5AxCiDILqYymiR2vwcXRc2XJN08WKjQIve7KMEfZjeWra1tCrWZMjqlMLdXC05E4CKtJVdWFKoKJrXIFSwtWKQ2RiQuz_f3yoD8qwSut7ysozAV12rc45CYJrHR6SZLhacHcraRaOe2KLvHALIdG7gziUtwr3JqL7NoIffeZuQwDBsd04l_FCXbHFkk_nGftY3hJPUCNQ6_CO9Hzr2XhJ4K_PloEaTo8jEiyR1oqk0FmFfZS7q0npJuNsMekxciPsY6Y4DPPs3ABlS4QhqTCfO9T4jjgQnPCnt4wVMngDPJEDq88oZyuu7yVxpkOTQbq5PgOG9n0hHGw3WxnEeby9JtulSaX-98D6-Rs8qkIoJOuIgTsUuQp8aqpIdvy3Ew0LbDmhWqV4LJ8YFdqaSqi7bwLe6-1w7JsJ1b-pDg" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v5cM1JDdhd_Gs5jKANeo7S4BOwUJSnREEmHyOi8kYfVImTAXkk1RHPhTvilD21-pVjXR78WvqDxY0e-Mury7sU8cOE297lL__tHOyqTaHgqsIPvL9MerpTLOziHPLop65CjfEoDTo5X8ZiXfZWRoNHQraxKvI-ZgXQNlxotoyA-BPBB5BHHmGzWP8pinJf4q7qoHTAv1vKyLMMcrJ7Ywfzc8I8MGEHxshfKIwriyKoLCcqbyk6mWpSiPHA0HkzyY3V_Z4L-FsytMD_oTdnZT9ORxkFZDfmuoZkvJt59uRE42eOy_2ybgT9D6xOTZHOJpWyUiLtW3KmWgyhL-9gkVz17b-qczXRui0sIreOT5LdE2ijj7ArprSJg3eGWK6R2b3qBab6XcMjDciE06GHkdf7oGBzi_TTfHsBK64CtqDFhAoz1o3EDmvqXtsezqt5mj0qTUEE5-8_hAXaSKB7-A8z7X6nu-fjOJVYk1bl-ENX3InjUkVFOx84eKDI5jA5aIUy_6O0zYziT6J-hgvGg6I0mAY5pMS3YxdUzJ0NtMZguwmMwBuCS-rzH8vn_XYAvx_lP5uVial6WcNa4kQH3vfvzNqhJdk5w2mazS2PXigrj8pSmWnp2hRPei3uKsvVrLlf317u808wLlunfsWmgFXiIecsaCzng4WtGnN-agpBf6BST8EBfXqP4T2nceW3XUVRXeNdtRg9roQ" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
