      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Iovis Statoris (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v6Sw-VyAnEl0gVS__4KiV6638iROmafSeIodZjOH6WDy637XUjg4BCqcxBotbmK1DJw7R-81jjQJCwOQMMv8glhhupXSDPMn23L6j-DwqqrgZHeCpVxdUhRp_fAfikCNj5kCPMUIe06aYMhf0noqbKll9rGiy9EWrMEGYeoGvUhTUxaCF3QDhRIrhgP_iZAtc7R1Mt6dWguOe7cZz-75OJh4FF_qN2JeE_19y740YsBseWSjbvSo7V53Ti_419EAAYZgRKDddz9oFoMq0zytPNyTlTmPUwqSk2dFaYKtfhaUzwO1hcYeRF4B-mX1tv5-VvEUqJ4JCdcITrQHXK6QGKH1g4ZQrkK15ibiAqiJE6_WH-tqoaCoSK-mMKpnFFut0lotc3HQ-IaCpceeF08byG1xqw-1AuK8VWrAr57E7OrME79D6jxuT05OOsecZIBOcmAThCKXR8qEoeNdfQg9Qy-XtVu_Ma4abZdtm3rKngulv32Ykr-a_ergHRhgHMiOmxOPGYSX6GF5ZYksysZBxMNqHJQ581MQVLBjD8SsQbDfuyvzA6--nwzmkk02NgY-l6paZzrVo-z3UI7kRhesEdYk3AoB7qvMNgNFEHhC2L8m80OFCcBpH1Cl5WhvjkCOTZMp6pEd0W3DzU1kEo7oPSUrfF-cFSkvwdcmYEPSwMZ4jVSXfyeMs0OemryShAOlnitASGTgcAG" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Temple of Jupiter Stator, Rome.<br><br>The Temple of Jupiter Stator was a temple named after the god Jupiter, in his form of Jupiter Stator (Jupiter the stayer). Together with the Temple of Juno Regina (Juno in the form of "Queen Juno") and the enclosing Porticus Metelli (later rebuilt as the Porticus Octaviae), it was built by Quintus Caecilius Metellus Macedonicus after his triumph, in 146 BC. <br><br>It is referred to as aedes Iovis Metellina and aedes Metelli. It was inside the porticus Metelli, close to the Circus Flaminius, and its exact site is known to have been beneath the church of Santa Maria in Campitelli. The Temple of Juno Regina was just west of it, on the opposite side of the Via della Tribuna di Campitelli.<br><br>It is not stated in explicitly by Velleius that Metellus built both temples, but that is the natural inference from the passage. He is also said to have been the first to build a temple in Rome entirely of marble, and which probably applies to both structures. In front of the temples Metellus placed Lysippus' equestrian statues of Alexander the Great's generals, and in them were several famous works of art.<br><br><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v5_ivII954_IXqTbnT3qG4tEHg0l5Tm20z4tocVucXmmnYNTkYXKC1sr268CZlH7bWHrWyhzg7oDhpj7HImlKnqDEtuDDzp10hrrfjJBWqRe7p2H79VixhyrcOR4S_t3vDI85KdKTdP6ftcjvXS2nk374UsGM_PEHpddfOUCaTww-3zbVHlHZa_yeuIVtirXJb0PWZPXU_tGM3B0sa9i8Tlr5fyUeLLQfYoVJFrmws0pjayZXF1Wapi7wSHmlXP3GtNwssuX8lek9cAJWzOty_ekfFl47svL9eH6454JJTzaT9-A61dseLmebQBX-Gv7Um5_3xFHbTRz8NKAjaBnCziahHaC7cqct_34JNJKWVVORf6KoMOwvBoJW6LmN6JCtgySzhRtngJtz6juSogrmiHs1BqcLVSFsgFTMgBIoe_-TCNjtBcOBzauoen9x2-yTcUcMZic9hwvXSye-_TUKHL7mxCaYdMC6czsq_r9iQgl3ceLX0ruB_olqhAKFKuEx5TaTfGusZq25ANn4F9V66IYUHzgtYK_XFmtvZ_DKe7sqjhJafDx5BpG0Z7sUKbsogNlvmX6wNRDSKsY9eUsPV6alPJ0lWyPUcoGKj78En1KU4br35WC1CfKB39dyL1t1-xTxKt530OTkIwJc3bcrxR1tfbU1gHk2RUcqAi486cbWEHOd-6Lueb4gYyaYxN49pnewZkmTAZzA" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
