      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Larium Permarini (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v5lPZVgNFMliARbpxx6xgxRdjJQEdUmBpbZ3SXM8law3AaNJb3gWxKjpiyRvhY9OzcJ22CiXj6bWLNQqwEDtA7qkEb7tlaL4Wx6XpVs8qYIPXvd7AMw2aO_XCX4OjbicAXuEQS6AOwUwbxeowO0DAJ0YV6wV9jTnBYPEcUYYtZgc7YG_G__13ETSE7ka3sE6wU_BotVteCayB8DH4rsjBJ8aU8lcUGK07Vwnhoh-UFl9RGwCjz6XRvaaRKjGdkCB4GOBqYR22T4u5g12shqj44YjUjetL6B0_DkDAd2Fciv25ScBM3XMlkG9c5tz15CZVXOiIdCxRY3sJB3OI9UOKdg6UUxOP-tzkhy18xmTFrVjuXtiHeD7j8h-sMmxAFzx0u9IgHSpEdi1ogmkv3gETuqQfxPbwKr7ww8rwsUrke-sXu4d1uSx_D3jO8QvLM-5Mi3t28a4pA_SEHbnrrec6no9SEon4jTAkJXZFvxqmU5gred1OZvC8s06mtsh5qPkWd2KEawyGA1lFGGBNnaIkExM0ELp_Ta39u2msZgvsfZ5PVTlsUvNRUxCZ5MRNN3NrpX8m-aESoPBJLTWaesinpOyGAi0lwj_JemCg0sCvYnFdekGBLoNq1f5v2mv0jim_oM-K37PLjZ0njl8aGP9cYBkHS4VIXbZP-ZO99h3UYFeVhWxQgte-z2O3ra8q02B4YbvbLCQw_i" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Temple of the Lares Permarini, Rome.<br><br>Votive temple of the 2nd c. BC to the Lares Permarini located in campo Martio, and more specifically by the fasti Praenestini in the Porticus Minucia ([LARIBVS PERM]ARINIS IN PORTI[CV MI]NVCIA. <br><br>Remnants of this temple were discovered in 1938 near the intersection of Via delle Botteghe Oscure and Via Celsa during a road-widening project; the remains, dating to the late 1st c. BC, correspond to a depiction of the temple on the Severan Marble Plan near the legend MINI[CIA].<br><br>The praetor L. Aemilius Regillus vowed the temple in 190 BC and L. Aemilius Lepidus dedicated it on 22 December 179 BC, along with his own temples in the Campus. Part of the dedicatory inscription affixed above the temple doors is preserved in Livy. Note that this temple stood immediately W of the point where the Porticus Aemilia (Campus Martius), which began at the Porta Fontinalis, debouched onto the Campus Martius; such a collocation of Aemilian dedications would easily explain the application of the name Aemiliana to this area.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1548-795548</styleUrl>
