      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Lunae (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Temple of Luna, Rome.<br><br>Temple of Luna on the Aventine, without identified remains. <br><br>Its site depends on that of the Temple of Ceres, whose location, though not known with certainty, can reasonably be narrowed to the lower slope of the Aventine’s N tip, just above the head of the Circus Maximus. Luna’s temple stood in the immediate vicinity of Ceres’, since its doors are reported to have been dislodged by a storm in 182 BC and hurled into the rear wall of the Temple of Ceres; further, both temples were hit by lightning — presumably the same bolt — on the same day in 84 BC. <br><br> The importance of a cult to Luna and the proximity of her temple to those of Ceres and Flora may appear less “obscure” when one takes into account the potentially destructive effect on crops and vegetation that the full moon was considered to have.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1548-795548</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            12.482314,41.887183,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Magnae Matris (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v53gC0hshnGWFuaY22LyEk1VJEf1cu7TpV0hLjLKKCaSoxOf3pqzvZMztLupE2dkziSaTOdU_75Njz6nHiotsXEdHCkpRTP3iwHA4a0Ky5M3c3tl91PMmnfqnscJIcE9m_W-BMWuVMYp3riDSzOEzQqV1nXy4MnOOxp2hc3_UtStbyCXfk9G6Glpei8FyZfcXW2qxbnx6pVtkD9dBUczvGRSHQIkthlP9HamGF3IrW2oDypMsdaPK4SYUUbr1s4enF4pTcNiDF914Ap_tgE3lhuemjGolGOs43y1eLjbwIax6wbzWoSbAJ8XJx7veosDD3DK0pT6aXNoABKoonTpXVdEAJJL_t3xCqY8nYOcIqsntslPAnj-qY7VkTjqW13HTd1MnMP4uJ5IfswWrPh7QN2QK-tn3DrHTIbkb9ghLrBGOYEWdusI7jcN3FwoVmVfhXsnoenqJyFNGSXbCfZ0FQBlNTxKMgYw8NJqVrDit0Jd5lcluAODzZKJNpJI6SAd3f3xZhjkhbtkhtXTKhLMVbDixRkPsyUikFsbYJP-M6f5JEQvurrPKm6Loa5uyaJ1I65ZuALscEh1Ib_FyRlKkIgx84iWxv0eguDgajGRraoiwQ4wb-huXbXqDbIrmuCzPXxnfkc7ce_gKPOnYF_kQyUPtFRRDu4Tj0ZzGa1UiU571Lq3eHwSDS4cZiPcTM66rD4oVe9NXBowA" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Temple of the Magna Mater, Rome.<br><br>Temple on the Palatine dedicated to the Phrygian mother-goddess Magna Mater, also known as Cybele, and home to the sacred black stone which represented the deity. <br><br>Begun in 204 and dedicated in 191 BC, the temple burned twice before it was restored by Augustus after the second fire of 3 AD.<br><br>Excavations on the SW corner of the Palatine in 1809 first brought the temple to light, while more recent investigations have clarified the architectural development of the structure. The extant remains, located just above the Scalae Caci and adjacent to the Temple of Victoria, indicate that the Augustan rebuilding utilized the earlier Republican foundations and high concrete podium (c. 33 x 17 m) to support a prostyle, hexastyle superstructure in the Corinthian order with a sculpted pediment. A statue of Magna Mater and inscriptions pertaining to her cult found in the vicinity allow these remains to be identified as her sanctuary.<br><br>Extending across the façade of the temple was a broad staircase, which led down to a large, paved platform where the ludi Megalenses, dramatic performances and games in honour of Cybele, were held; these steps would have seated spectators. Sometime after the fire of 111 BC, modest vaults extended this precinct across a street, here identified as the Clivus Victoriae, that had previously limited the platform on the SW; tabernae (small shops and offices) opening onto the street were located within the barrel-vaulted spaces below the platform.<br><br><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v6Mm2GTJavVxgUEQ1D4m72YyqBseFR8rrodyFo4IkD4ZB8MoQWk7eQrecMhZiMJIwwf2gLczoIZdKmA-WAxvzcAkJDRt2QABFkj3A1cQ-mReFvve6i5A_7IfEHlQEvFaCOlSxqIbUk1DJfpU6oqdPLxAtTLw9N-hAYp-30akEKr3K0K-IZYU3SfFGaiWQzmd67RVGTb1mkDG3J1j_3MSdEM-EoeXFXAP2fLOiwiJr1L3PXuV9MNuSbitRBj3OpmKYJSmGdSLXT-iIglLcAiNrsWaS4pws__J5DiChdoZ69racaqiWoPzWfAbyDr7whUBoo-p5I_tMOSbohW3Ss3AjtiZREUiLxodux1xrW83YbHTvhY6rtE24s3nfamLfY5hByMYCzsV96efYRG92BesTpuszK1j98j__GfXjoL7_ycMpEAm-QmLg3cmdYY8z0-z7YnkK-SGOXJmB6bUdZlzR7MRWSKJG8ZWAYfmHI7Pac_SbdElkRDE_CgR2kgJW1PsIGfe9XBI_Ie4Uq8ww_-YIj5snH3ReDTh90EJpBpr6avySW733QxftFJ_iyrL8_XAwxXuW7pZk5CA0qlwOQKjfvUk_Km_z35rM9y-_2MJP8TXKfHw-mQzu1CPKjne8eHSgUetRiKJLkxmYkq0mpAEVJwx6nVOEh4EismoJM_1JBCKhEAIaOgaN6TviWyigawSsfSnJ4-PFUQIw" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
