      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Opis (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v4s1c4qIePM7x6BOm_PiCPI4-kfRcivjGR-8Ig71o_2jGLpzXNsfNwb3Se6Md7f7gY2fmRpnzWrrj37YWUCHQvwj-HqN0iEyHcoWiHrlrf6CyTZRubadwWKrnPfEEGUnef-oHmJNdx8bRNu2bIRV9b_iz9qFFzp26JlD4GX8k8S9izBUfepxmsBElsHcj3HX2GOi4U5oLafpACU6JV7h7hn7t7kgKgmzGybx-sSaNb3x8xCsW-rWmuk2rM5mMRgVU_gsESHHX6olPbstLl3d07_cTavLv3TAw6jQ01BBKqJV3LluhRS2knmBUgPL3n1kDX1ijvwDGJ5iDjp8a_wI8CoTadpgpJu9nqtI9Wtj7GgGQg8oCAMHDPW9HiRJ2FubZWlj8U2m7hFWce0mLvjZQK6f7lLZhAAwbPeSE0XLASFacvnYQ9Gd1G1IoZND37mJK8xjoxbdvUaBW0njUgRvTpr4Z8w3AiJPUNQKijf8TIfLP0eZkeekGOIW5nu8kMrxF1zPztqzIBjuBJWJgvMbwJDiZhrmo3mt21aD3qrVRpJ9_v-kOyj3BwQp0OEQzWPJrDfIe0ULTuWtsS6nOQV1Sd55Fj3djTVhkaYhNj7eCM43uvQImkkSn73jSn4MnKv8eCb-3QVvMPBHxDog4gYhnEVxv9u6JV4QUYbfoKKzjcO1qjNmrM4JT3ii51nfmOG_XIToF2cCLRqEQ" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Temple of Ops, Rome. <br><br>A mid-Republican temple of Ops, the goddess of wealth, stood in Capitolio and was struck by lightning in 186 BC. It was probably dedicated by L. Caecilius Metellus in 250 BC.<br><br> It existed in the Augustan period, for it was here that women and children assembled for the celebration of the ludi Saeculares of 17 BC. The Temple of Ops is believed to have stood next to the Temple of Fides: military diplomas of the 1st c. AD were attached to both temples; a storm in 44 BC damaged both temples, and the concepts of fides and ops (faith and wealth) were closely related.]]></description>
