      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Penatium Publici (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Temple of the Penates Publici, Rome.<br><br>Temple to the Penates Publici, located on the Velia, was rebuilt by Augustus. <br><br>The Altar of Pax Augusta may offer visual evidence for the appearance of the shrine; the relief of Aeneas sacrificing includes an image of the enshrined Lavinian Penates in the background which closely corresponds to the description of the Roman Temple of the Penates Publici found in Dionysius of Halicarnassus; perhaps the sculptors found their model for the relief in the recently renewed temple.<br><br>The temple was probably destroyed during the fire of 64 AD and subsequent Neronian rebuilding on the Velia. ]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1548-795548</styleUrl>
