      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Solis (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v5hPiqelpTn8hokks_mL28Uh0uiCj-4NQEq5eavk6LoEpbppzJISFZOtEDNeIYFjnZPCgX2J_QRK9OBYezNZCtXgpQ1bBtlESw4eaMBGmE8kE3pkzdafuzPPz3aj9eYheUY17JP73C4zGbKKjkKVwx3PLSZL4gJUCoU7Tj_pGu3GOXnnYl9jd9e60G0_hrJHsreXrU8ckf_0mdU51wdBJwhChNWpvB7Phg8CvWTmrFJdLf9o2zHl7i0gTmNOyqmpqUOyLmiCxWK2caTZzPeb7awEDJHUswjtrY1aNwSwobv8VbO0DXa6kGwmxPMhekDprQ7Deu3pKEzSb69ixofYns5u6oX_UF17SOUZEJWsCbIsFrN6zs1o85y-8ZuOoVqxaYpnsSuPO1LK26eebbu4nXXkZBTugzB191H1X60L4M2d-P4rIZmu0C3Zc3LXRDF8owKbgrXNjxayNZ0b-mP-AEDgdlNP3KCp6WefWXSlZgCOEFciFr-G-VvG413lgU_ssil6AmALxi0Gks2cPdAv9pMsGraXUxkEe3lO1O5yWHb6ITEkk6_IGfVuBz3vHc6AfebRcldIyyultUf3Ihv_nMQwnegKJVG7ucD-Gz9zIV0AC1XIMyqZ2pJZJNqhDfxBIF8vvzlSdrHcrTuqvst54Iie7C_DsqsrnlbXuv905QhJ8FNjwtfo6Mi3L-6FREZBcwA0URCF0zrIw" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Temple of Sol, Rome.<br><br>Archaic temple within the Circus Maximus dedicated to the sun-god Sol, to whom the Circus as a whole was consecrated; the temple was embedded in the seating on the Aventine side, just opposite the finish line and across from the Pulvinar.<br><br> Tacitus, in the first secure reference to the temple, calls it a vetus aedes in 65 AD; earlier numismatic testimony may be found on a denarius of Mark Antony dated to 42 BC, which depicts a small, distyle shrine to Sol.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1548-795548</styleUrl>
