      <Placemark>
        <name>Templum Veneris Erycinae (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Temple of Venus Erycina, Rome.<br><br>Extra-urban Temple to Venus Erycina near the Porta Collina, vowed in 184 BC by L. Porcius Licinius and dedicated in 181 BC by his son of the same name.<br><br>The extramural location would have facilitated the celebration of erotic cult practices, including the presence of cult prostitutes. Though no architectural remains survive, a denarius minted by C. Considius Nonianus at Rome in 57 BC, which depicts the Sicilian shrine with a tetrastyle façade and triangular pediment, is suggestive.<br><br>The temple was the site of the Vinalia festival held on April 23. The fasti list both April 23 and October 24 as the dies natalis.]]></description>
