      <Placemark>
        <name>Domus C. Sestii (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Residence, Rome.<br><br>Republican residence of C. Sestius located in the Subura on the Argiletum, and known from an inscription marking the extent of the property that was found in situ in the basement of a house near S. Maria dei Monti in 1628. A wall of opus reticulatum was seen adjacent to the inscription.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1603-A52714</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            12.491257,41.894601,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Domus Cn. Calpurnii Pisonis (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Residence, Rome.<br><br>The home of the prominent Augustan consular and longtime friend of Tiberius, Cn. Calpurnius Piso, described by Tacitus as ‘overhanging the Forum’.<br><br> A recently-published inscription from Spain refers to certain structures ‘which Piso built over the Porta Fontinalis in order to join private houses’, which were demolished by the decree of the Senate in 20 AD in the wake of Piso’s disgrace following the death of Germanicus. This location fits well with Tacitus’ wording, since the pre-Trajanic geography of the area between the Quirinal and the Arx, where the Porta Fontinalis stood, was high enough in relation to the neighbouring Forum to provide the visual prominence that a powerful Senator’s residence required.<br><br>It is unclear how we should reconstruct this structure’s ground-plan from its description. The inscription refers specifically to additions built by Piso to merge more than one separate domus into a single complex. The language used seems to suggest something built over, i.e. on top of, the gate itself, perhaps connecting houses on either side of the city wall. Alternatively, the preposition ‘supra’ may simply refer to the general location of the structures in question, and need not suggest that Piso’s domicile actually impinged upon a public structure. In either case, no remains have yet been found.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1603-A52714</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            12.484494,41.894426,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Domus Corneliae L. f. (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Residence, Rome.<br><br>Residence of Cornelia from the Augustan period located on the Quirinal under the large exedra of the thermae Diocletianae. The name is attested on a fistula aquaria recovered with the remains of an early-Imperial building, which Coarelli dates to the Augustan period. This Cornelia was probably the wife of L. Volusius Saturninus, cos. suff. in  3 AD and later praefectus urbi.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1603-A52714</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            12.49636,41.902746,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Domus Flavia (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v7IET5I1K00TwhUiYGzvvUrUq-I3eUQB95noMgRe7uSLbk0NkLNgPuHMu6qZnzFW8VqEwTdcsqyXBFPV8lpMzHhIQus5ZTtvUmBr-uZUqrEs3ivuh5GuRrf9SdO1zAGgd1xf0iHhfLzNDwAEFqkCoK1vlvwBN3QaZpsGkUmPpctOWxzdOCOB9movc1Dtm5WqYibf2IeHFwVQ_VIgrEZOTTaT3nJYNpixR5VxzlwZoxyNUeprXkEAdTe7fuvpqfe8LjpY-xz-g2T78xCvIkQ_MfyNp0P4Catrgzlfziaai_EG6QQ4r0VLcvHFO9jnEoatKs4K5HIYqHz4n6EbGkfDJoSl-vgN00AxZk-SqmuTUCKgJaupRfBVuNaZEfqiqnHVNrVZd_RaQBndqXqiPXpYjDUZNbQTm64fFRN_V9CQLBS5eVkDVWZkJInDl49P_ZY5WWFT_XkHHy7vDh49jN6DWpYl8TegTBsmevQu9zDRuTIme5Nb3yY21zwL5eQNLE-7BZzkgITNszOTY_YP7T3ebKDTEHQkg6ySF5ypcFXvBtWCUzE747wrE3QFgCbBXHRznCFUPLcTm2idS4t1GEspt0DQ_HNYs8Ks1BRRy_TlM9gup_jHxZxqd3MW_9PlNw0T5ovlLUrVTSckx0to8We8ptFzLXKwXxN_EH1UJNjihfV3xn0pUzXMWHWqVZTRELcIurPKQY3uVPjCQ" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Imperial Palace, Rome.<br><br>The Flavian Palace, normally known as the Domus Flavia, is part of the vast residential complex of the Palace of Domitian on the Palatine Hill in Rome. It was completed in 92 AD by Emperor Domitian, and attributed to his master architect, Rabirius.<br><br>The term Domus Flavia is a modern designation used to describe the northwestern section of the Palace where the bulk of the large public rooms for entertaining and ceremony are concentrated. It is interconnected with the domestic wing to the southeast, the Domus Augustana, which descends from the summit of the Palatine down to wings specially constructed within the hill to the south and southwest.<br><br>The imposing ruins which flank the southeastern side of the Palace above the Circus Maximus are a later addition built by Septimius Severus; they are the supporting piers for a large extension which completely covered the eastern slope.<br><br><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v64X6aEEljOck_ROjKkmDDVGRtHXosCEFffD0ay2oYfFPanzK1qr8sx9H_ytVvWlbWFnPcV1rjiAa5ov8U-b9w-n8GyGnmwU3DAWh_NR_CQZP6DXrtro5lbd-lYh3T1yRO9sLVIdCJShIF9_FvhxQzuYWUxDMGhh1JC4oniUTAFAi45ReBd789JfqVAWGRG_l1CZr5MShINQraEZFahO6JAXTiOaJ2Or_CwtmGdRWK3regR_JSaGMmECc36jamAFXl7GaSMOrZUx6moWM-jXBUMS96KsCPOb9PDrKiK4N3-G8iDQ44ys2AMvO2Xp1Nql-dua1XP9gfufxDT5bNV6ZpOOP-eSEjJH5Ogp-4h7W5Xuqz4QpZECHpTsFupF_KBvUynGbUvHBzzjJ1mYHWeKCT_-gPaO_1CO3X8jUsjV6SKCFxK6_hTo8AxG0a66GYNXJ_dnXtp2Af_ExviyZJrTGiErTgfQdpZcbNZ5vqRAY__FujSHhB0RqxPp3DURTrN45Ty-2LFYLzsbhBqqXFSaNrg12ZWg2JYcAQCG0ctp4kqpqydCs0S2VloiRTfCVdjbZRo5cKAh1u9s4vQoeV1Vx0L0EbfafRueOAr85Z8flV2r4XtdpRalDfR--ylvCyNA3RhsZvMKFg6xoR_khVmFg95vP2CqAwROpg9Xt5OlkJSJ5I-7_HHilgU1fgbVdHYOt9gN1L3m0bf" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/umsh/AN6v0v7-cbpoHKwll9CZZ_cnWcFUeaw1YuDlKIeSn1KpExH2bhp1JuzGBXgLJaHVao6o_N5ieCW61I6EboFcxSY7zARN59974BHePiSJv_09TodFLo7hjsgXvVu9uvKYhVCium_yD6N_ikYIwwmo4X9_49W6gNqVjSG9rnx4zP8vlnF7OFM_17YMj9N-Cd0HP5zedbsJ7HFzNQn4Qs80ZAIy4ugiAQgs6_azS2unYJAX_zEZ1sfzQzDiN6O1_qP34hXeIsM84IHaTONChbdBxElvbwYdGJTK_sAjPC-8rAPUfAjPO2VhoQwvfEZzaj_HZJ_Wb199mXvC6_eeBjExwTina_p6Ae6U5xpWMpVxX2wzR2-J8KmWCaXGvqTRSDKm67CNGlES4WgBIImaM34XoKr8tBpsyqkXFBBaz3rb0ME70LnEOD5v_UY80LmTVuuw2AHZCo6GPo5Quu05hhYH7Q91XrtXSwVTncyZZ5CSaNKR5g1EkjR-0Itu8yWIZoxK1cf6_SW_KxKmjSVGmvm5LbRJaM3NBOg6MGm56Zew099Ueteai4pGURS7QL1QG3MBokxnnf-HDChI6D0A4v_qlR9I__NYRkcp4Yj5FhvzPt2fsUSe1FpTdOkoiZNQskcm7huNd7wOdioOk9s0WyGJel-YQFwXMjS8pgA8Ff-zkmB6amF9zWwU-3ncIw9gytdl27PCd9SuUJ1WP6_seA" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
