      <Placemark>
        <name>Domus Sessoriana (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gys2f6JbQy3sP2DvMqU1mQbwdLVnfr20d91VDBgyxFV-UlNnyuEh1O7Cl-qNLavElNm6qP-HZZr21tyUwm84A0ZmEwgQ_oTJ9MTwG2c9vpr8EI74GJ_Hi2yh5dVk5U9PmIj_CxwSQ-Umu7D1N6823ei4blmkrY_CU3Vh5G8x9azCoVF5nVG_9xR4SJHC5fiTEU6vodO61PYXA?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Imperial Palace, Rome.<br><br>The Sessorium, a building known in later times as the palatium Sessorianum, was standing in the 1st c. AD when it is mentioned as being near the spot where the execution of criminals took place. The origin of the name is unexplained, but the building became an imperial residence in the 4th c. AD and was a favourite home of Helena, the mother Constantine.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1671-673AB7</styleUrl>
