      <Placemark>
        <name>Villa Capitis Tauri (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GzllyW2iCJgXj2vWcUdYoMktXsGsE0Zj-WqkAcHmVQ5Jmj9lY3Dz64KjXnEgPwsCrl61sxNzZxu93V-V-HXJB424px5YdPDwf0tk7Ug177rFyXbymKn9SFky1JJxk-KnxqS2WvzVVTN2AzZjGCf29oiDH_Su0sDJXRI2yTOpkJ96LVflcceWvfOn-Cs3GSZ74r2_1Tgkhb_0w?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Country house, Rome.<br><br>The villa was owned by Herodes Atticus and his wife Annia Regilla. The excavations revealed thermal baths dating back to the middle of the 2nd c. AD. These baths were used until at least the 4th c. AD and were almost certainly for private use. Greek inscriptions found there remind us of the Greek origins of Herodes Atticus. There are several well-preserved mosaics and the high quality of building materials used suggest a very elegant environment. Water was provided by two large cisterns.<br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GwuBDrCLVm8qG8OePcvYdXJaAtM7pKpwIzSPyU2H9_WIU_0kq-UsxUbBPx13KQyiL0F-mnuAk-mnaiXiLEInPmENoBnB_Sd5k-dWudE6kNhPriumj9NKGzjxEFexQBDrevS_jrszcOnHVQgHogC7Ww-NGqZpCDGf3VFD84zeFHFyyqUv2HQyGYKMZeoiQf0jsJC6qeAkr7HjA?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1603-A52714</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GzllyW2iCJgXj2vWcUdYoMktXsGsE0Zj-WqkAcHmVQ5Jmj9lY3Dz64KjXnEgPwsCrl61sxNzZxu93V-V-HXJB424px5YdPDwf0tk7Ug177rFyXbymKn9SFky1JJxk-KnxqS2WvzVVTN2AzZjGCf29oiDH_Su0sDJXRI2yTOpkJ96LVflcceWvfOn-Cs3GSZ74r2_1Tgkhb_0w?authuser=0&fife=s16383 https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GwuBDrCLVm8qG8OePcvYdXJaAtM7pKpwIzSPyU2H9_WIU_0kq-UsxUbBPx13KQyiL0F-mnuAk-mnaiXiLEInPmENoBnB_Sd5k-dWudE6kNhPriumj9NKGzjxEFexQBDrevS_jrszcOnHVQgHogC7Ww-NGqZpCDGf3VFD84zeFHFyyqUv2HQyGYKMZeoiQf0jsJC6qeAkr7HjA?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
