    <Folder>
      <name>Industry/Trade</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Atria Licinia (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Auction halls, Rome.<br><br>Auction halls near the entrance of the Macellum mentioned by Cicero.<br><br> No remains of the Atria Licinia have been found, but Cicero’s reference to the fauces Macelli implies a location somewhere behind the E façade of the Basilica Paulli.]]></description>
