      <Placemark>
        <name>Forum Espuilinum (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Commerical area, Rome.<br><br>Commercial space on the S Cispian. <br><br>Appian’s description of a battle said to have taken place here in 88 BC between C. Marius and L. Sulla implies that the Forum Esquilinum was a large open space, located just inside the Porta Esquilina. It is mentioned in several funerary inscriptions. An inscription discovered by the Church of S. Vito, built on the site of the Porta Esquilina, mentions a forum restored by Fl. Eurycles Epitychianus in 450 AD. The findspot of this inscription suggests that the Forum Esquilinum stood inside the Porta Esquilina, N of the Clivus Suburanus. The Macellum Liviae, which was built outside the Porta Esquilina during the Augustan period, confirms the commercial nature of this area.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1684-A52714</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
