      <Placemark>
        <name>Columbaria Statiliorum Taurorum (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Tombs of the Statilii Tauri, Rome.<br><br>The agglomeration of columbarium-tombs of the Statilii Tauri, their freedmen and slaves, formed the core of a large necropolis N of the ”Via Labicana-Praenestina”, close to Spes Vetus. <br><br>Excavations from 1875 to 1877 have resulted in an extensive collection of funerary inscriptions and an overall ground-plan. Some parts of the necropolis may be dated with certainty to the Augustan period or earlier. A small columbarium in opus reticulatum may be dated, on the basis of wall frescoes with scenes from the Aeneas legend, to the 1st c. BC. <br><br>The tomb of Q. Pompeius Sosus, whose name appears on the epitaph, dates to around 50 BC; its peperino blocks were reused as foundations for later columbaria. The funerary inscription of two slaves of Autronius Paetus was found in the area; their master was either the consul of 66 BC or his son, the consul of 33 BC, hence we can be sure that this area was in use during the Augustan period. <br><br>Close by stood the main columbarium of the Statilii Tauri, in use from the time of Augustus to Claudius. Slaves and freedmen of the Statilii are attested nearby; it is likely that these columbaria were built at the same time. <br><br>As for the rest of the necropolis, the evidence is less clear. Some columbaria remained in use until the time of Nero, yet this does not rule out an earlier construction date. As a general rule, those areas discovered at a depth of c. 9 m are considered Augustan or earlier, while those at c. 6 m are early Imperial.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1556-A52714</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            12.514467,41.891647,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Columbarium (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Tomb, Rome.<br><br>A columbarium was unearthed in 1936 during works to expand the modern Via Nomentana near its intersection with Via Asmara. <br><br>The remains included a series of structures in opus reticulatum pertaining to an underground sepulchral chamber with niches for cinerary urns. The names of the deceased are not preserved.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1556-A52714</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            12.507053,41.91398,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Columbarium Libertorum Augusti (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GxqhRGG_iQSUvug4_AVbmDFeKsdNjD9wOVB29X37b9iQoiW3QxVKiqEmVzqfxKPEsAN92m3wT3ECl1FueXIpz_uWElciltK962TtO1xvQo-_qX5x5M7nzSNTA3Em0hfK60sxcusLY4Hz7El2wcytAJiMzbuE2Mw4GWJu_fDQiMG6DyA7Qfgf5dPtZdMH2dCKFknhFzRZdmHStw?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Tomb of Augustus' freedmen, Rome.<br><br>It was discovered on the second mile of via Appia in 1724-26 in the course of excavations of the columbarium of the freedmen of Livia.<br><br>An overground construction of 3 adjacent chambers was coated with bricks and covered with plaster. It housed c. 3000 niches, each for 2 ceramic urns in the form of pots.<br><br>In 1747 the current state of the building was studied and fixed in a series of etchings by G. B. Piranesi.<br><br>In 1790 Carlo Labruzzi made another etching of the monument.<br><br>In 1796 the Vatican made a census of the taverns of the city for defining a number of tax-payers. According to this census the taverna inside the ruins of the columbarium was named Hosteria del colombario. At the present time the ruins are occupied by a restoraunt “Hostaria Antica Roma”.<br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GxEb5jX9JVGKXgRot3LGK2CL0Sk_d1kSlQnHfxu8hMw_JQc3Inveyo745h0nid0s-qrgoen4zG58VYzzxTxEbl8tdpO_LKHkATOuoM6dxxg9N6-HJRLZK42bNgIbAe5qs9Nl2F5e1HlsfsZtpLS8q0-FLkbH1mTeipy2Opv5NhnZ_C5RNoVbPNTMcxNdAVS0tp_gTPqx0GUS8o?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gy5AV9Z6yLo_hwjH_ea0dIu_3pnwveOQDyWW85ZT2Ee3YagBcsCI3TxcLHyH2KstHu38nqEkoyRghKK1N_lOAc5Wv7tpxJ3RssC7rVoqI2h-ZD8XuEK9R8PuFQWinrmehw3vhZLMm_BMt5UkzLB7lYEVNTj5jiWdr-Q5nyrbMe64LHfNRWlDBvhMk0u7nis6GiCVqjFnyi-eu4?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gxtct4rwipE-roWDgRjJsl49kEC6hPNgiT3mY8kbGgeBsy41dRoUE2eCg42zeNTByeb3S0dzO7IecGqK19XzNdaTi8Hex6zrCEHo6s6eJX-TA7qeyUfD5rNS84O64aFn35Daqo3BQH4YbZDbGTyBkjaaub6LN565YaJwtqYimABwv4mwC0YKe4tgiy4f1EbpWge96sToKE1Am0?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1556-A52714</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
