      <Placemark>
        <name>Mausoleum Romuli (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GwVeyxGFnWkcxohB_24h4F4pTnZ4FdO7vyDl2T_scNhRDHUL2NbTebHMKwAfS_64f-qThW4FoZJTCzVYDoyOYWcQ8uoHDxxllvJ4qm3Mya_f7gA4gKQWkCt5Lj5iF6aybqltfnGzYn6twdggaGn_7jPhMdfzJmC063MfK2cSufiqm7ZYauMLdZx6Ap-vKO5-IZAghRsEQ89iw?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Tomb of Romulus, Rome.<br><br>The large circular tomb was built by the emperor Maxentius in the early 4th c. AD, probably with himself in mind and as a family tomb, but when his young son Valerius Romulus died he was buried there first and it was dedicated to him.<br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GwmuRYk3cFn8eyCfGfGs5PFi9wGYN2dFvJJIlrYH8PW-EGJ8yOa-YE25RwZQV34tHStKOisLuqQiVMIeT4ocRyowhZGFBNxTVh_Iv4ewmmGCwWXcsrZy2gab-5afGxdof1An766TsMtjyINN24DjOUHt2pF9RPTEwoyngEQk3wL01XD5YjH2lWwjR5YZ_hNWnVJz0ezIee6yQ?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
