      <Placemark>
        <name>Sepulcrum Corneliae L. Scipionis f. (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Tomb of Cornelia, Rome.<br><br>Tomb for Cornelia, daughter of L. Scipio, and wife to a Vatienus, located well outside the Servian Wall along the Via Salaria.<br><br> Traditionally, the tomb inscription is associated with a circular Augustan tumulus monument revetted in marble, which was uncovered when the porta Salaria was destroyed in 1871. The demolition work revealed extensive remains, including an opus caementicium nucleus and numerous carved elements of the superstructure in travertine and marble. The style of the bucrania and lettering suggest a date of c. 40-30 BC.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1556-A52714</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            12.498074,41.910798,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Sepulcrum Corneliorum Scipionum (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GzsQhg9G5OxHJkGmAS7dlFo_F63ypEazwGoz-lscfZ9yauiiwqdfGIzwMqdt_4nl8KyTY08-cIImLoP_UKci96sWOBjzPUYVfBzBDMclGoY3R8OYVnUclxDFHPlSEHZclJBiatvSbF08OaQqKhDe0okyquxaHRQW3qosoChyIzpLw6VPEm3bgTfIyX3pZrdO5JBl35AuakHGg?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Tomb of the Cornelii Scipiones, Rome.<br><br>Family tomb of the Cornelii Scipiones, which faced onto a minor cross street connecting the Via Appia with the Via Latina, about 1 km outside the Porta Capena.<br><br> One of the most illustrious tombs of the city, it was originally built in the 3rd c. BC, when an irregular square chamber (c. 13.5 x 14.5 m) was cut into the living rock to house the family’s sarcophagi, many of which survive.<br><br> Over time, the internal chambers of the tomb were expanded (to hold over 30 burials), and in the 2nd c. BC a new, monumental columnar façade was erected. It was probably at that point that the tomb was adorned with statues of P. Cornelius Scipio Africanus (cos. 205, 194 BC), L. Cornelius Scipio Asiaticus (cos. 190 BC), and the poet Q. Ennius.<br><br>With the extinction of the Cornelii Scipiones in the early 1st c. BC, the tomb was inherited by the Cornelii Lentuli, who reused it briefly under Claudius for the burial of Cornelia Gaetulica and M. Iunius Silanus Lutatius Catulus, respectively the wife and nephew of Lentulus Gaetulicus (cos. 26 AD).<br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GzzDFrbKDyGZjwtQxhYPkzCfMk3YGSjKQtCJ7MO5x3j9JSvvDElL8g15JjTfuXXA_VjbRZd0CjfLqAzG8KsbpNBQGg_oVdnoqaMS3iNW-JNJwrmT2PZ5VVaydUSapNiyb1H2jSI_PBPk0CodFRpA8vLdQrQbxiZtnrm8QkLRKFNEz6r21W7F2ZHoiZdbfF9uH46Ojuor0_jGw?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GxzQzy3P34S68kjDzs1SKzo6ZmxUkysjTdvM5ANBeAZzIlB_XwBlETsI-vU3D4ZHmuPEH9GV3CT8ml5pfbkVjFThN1PhMvfZ-oK3rIGUX4bvSBU06n_Pzj6ljS9qMaoHmS9YniEzZdDFL1OP-dQOd2hCMoyXMlTVts_spzXO5d6iWbe95XZ07OEbGBVr1hrs7NSg3ECSVMkqw?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GzrkMJN89fKKH_bh1tFyhRvt2DwY01si69Vu-_YIuPPqbdPItVPJB7rTRs9lzR9iogoCI-KR8to7nm8eEmIu0rxZiXTFERKDrhZYadxz2svUrXlvyjG64ks3d3wK1e32DFVPhj-X015zMGAjRp0A3PHaHAHkSbbBXP8GktUpwIeeofw1nZdSELC-ct_NMHHeJ34tWAlR9eMbA?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gw9ZUtzbuG1nqtnvGlDfuh6-PoX93UNWXucjgKbyw5FgjzwjUXKN1dl_PcnA1KXJ3MjhFI8hNBSycDUlifvgWrpX5B9M0kCnSvrv16mAkTZoqXr4QTewBOtzhwjJzy3jwI1GCtMdADcuReHSLbIWHJbuY__fOcgzjVXhHUM2HlLNYENSd3PuCkGmGRa6d33_zHec1n958G7OQ?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gwv9V6LXGOmL15mIUJ4O2ULKXbhFPu1_V6Ih9vDcai6XRJR9kIJzUP8DlygxcD_mJ6F3_F2oA4ZDFr8GPKEQU62jdI2svdkAEd_Cf7utSC6PD9RylyMC7UYlNynloMJxEPw7OiCUHne3eXQgKGhw3VLmD5dcHn0sfkxUOpflYLljE0-sFS-RyMW_0iQLn9Jwiy4V8ZecWnE2g?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
