          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Sepulcrum M. Aemilii Dulionis (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Tomb of M. Aemilius Dulio, Rome.<br><br>Remains of a tufa mausoleum in opus quadratum were found on the W side of Via Salaria along with an inscribed marble slab naming the tomb’s proprietor, M. Aemilius Dulio. The tomb lay at the far E edge of the “Sepulcra Salaria”.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1556-A52714</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            12.497648,41.912602,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Sepulcrum M. Lucilii Paeti (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Tomb of M. Lucilius Paetus, Rome.<br><br>Tumulus-style tomb built on the Via Salaria by M. Lucilius Paetus, who held the offices of tribunus militum, praefectus fabrum and praefectus equitum under Augustus, for himself and his sister in c. 20 BC.<br><br> A ring of travertine ashlar masonry (diam. 34.9 m) and a burial chamber survive; originally the tomb was crowned by an earthen tumulus akin to the Mausoleum of Augustus. The tomb is the largest and most luxurious monument known in the “Sepulcra Salaria”.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1556-A52714</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            12.496602,41.914969,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Sepulcrum M. Servilii Quarti (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GyvfbtvqWpULw2nBTymNucep_PDqoBSnoDNPn8yxiVskEUb_VoQDcimop5z56b1FMdT4o3awV8wY5ZpbLIsWuL1cDjzQS63eZ5vh7BAT6kLUzKkkR5yxGgoLw_c-jV1zer_KvlCHVtxvFW66oKfN40Ot_tfWBb3doiLcrLDk4_d5VznsX1kmTCUXyJAyJCKuyoyqyJvzYa0Jw?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Tomb of M. Servilius Quartus, Rome.<br><br>The tomb of M. Servilius Quartus made on bricks on the Via Appia and was restored in 1808.<br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GyL_poUc7M9lBTxGblXysFdaYpeXIQvz-QOam8rs-j87TBX9CsrIk3yAbdBvo3RUUJvH0iELbVbYUb52CczN32Qn9m42VS3lPDpVRpMFq5lllM4t2Tt64fTpitZ8T5uwmvS_bY38Qw0V7r-BsjvK86KmXcH9JwE6uCa67-OsV_qEC6feMs936-XAha9AoBDYPoJZhVuYSSXNw?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1556-A52714</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GyvfbtvqWpULw2nBTymNucep_PDqoBSnoDNPn8yxiVskEUb_VoQDcimop5z56b1FMdT4o3awV8wY5ZpbLIsWuL1cDjzQS63eZ5vh7BAT6kLUzKkkR5yxGgoLw_c-jV1zer_KvlCHVtxvFW66oKfN40Ot_tfWBb3doiLcrLDk4_d5VznsX1kmTCUXyJAyJCKuyoyqyJvzYa0Jw?authuser=0&fife=s16383 https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GyL_poUc7M9lBTxGblXysFdaYpeXIQvz-QOam8rs-j87TBX9CsrIk3yAbdBvo3RUUJvH0iELbVbYUb52CczN32Qn9m42VS3lPDpVRpMFq5lllM4t2Tt64fTpitZ8T5uwmvS_bY38Qw0V7r-BsjvK86KmXcH9JwE6uCa67-OsV_qEC6feMs936-XAha9AoBDYPoJZhVuYSSXNw?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
