      <name><![CDATA[Roads & Walls]]></name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Muri Aureliani (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GxE3nZ6ZeXRWP94IM0TfKI1TNY-r7UZXLByBdDpkTPvhGMy78mG-vwxlf9OAovFpwJ22X-W-jMTc0kbCnJJEp0HAg49VTYYtZiq_33l3JIOU64OWViOdBwrmUNW5tjelMYfTIkhzO00kVqioygIjWo5Pw9ezDobl19dvuTqswMpGOspVkB6WCwW8y0RPbO86ikNjkGLVlMLrg?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Aurelian Walls, Rome.<br><br>The Aurelian Walls are a line of city walls built between 271-275 AD in Rome during the reign of Emperors Aurelian and Probus. They superseded the earlier Servian Wall built during the 4th c. BC.<br><br>The walls enclosed all the seven hills of Rome plus the Campus Martius and, on the right bank of the Tiber, the Trastevere district. The river banks within the city limits appear to have been left unfortified, although they were fortified along the Campus Martius. The size of the entire enclosed area is 1,400 hectares (3,500 acres).<br><br>The actual effectiveness of the wall is disputable, given the relatively small size of the city's garrison. The entire combined strength of the Praetorian Guard, cohortes urbanae, and vigiles of Rome was only about 25,000 men – far too few to defend the circuit adequately. However, the military intention of the wall was not to withstand prolonged siege warfare; it was not common for the barbarian armies to besiege cities, as they were insufficiently equipped and provisioned for such a task. Instead, they carried out hit-and-run raids against ill-defended targets. The wall was a deterrent against such tactics.<br><br>Parts of the wall were doubled in height by Maxentius, who also improved the watch-towers. In 401, under Honorius, the walls and the gates were improved. At this time, the Tomb of Hadrian across the Tiber was incorporated as a fortress in the city defenses.<br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gxic4Gz5gsaxqPJgR5-RBjRGZjEzk-tHmx_2gBJFM8d0qenfavTEcIhIRJbwRGnbVzTmfVf2WCPBdgj0gp5qrXiV4QCWiPjVtSAleIffFwzvqIG_4YA0kyyJve8RYO2U4-5UQ3-o8kt9TnbEXMPQ1RNpmbu6HzYiqgjgnXeQlFlz8MMTv7Ak7cxAjOGm32_l9S3Z1Zmx8SnLw?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GxyTHrwCh6jj7f_kE-xL3TXa0c9ryCNinHtSuw5BKgCsn_ucf00Blx_C2l5ExoSSELYveCqVOn32yns_L0x50it6O-4I3ZeX8nrQRpmB3X8GZUmigoM5G7mtZrytXC80rwAnK764-C1bV7rSjS8OT3wdVXpEqyHoY3hIWTNXJoDI9S6A0DKompNv7-bHNA37_xb1RWyf_Y6WA?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GyqXmU9mJwx6KttZdv2fpLkJKPnBWDyJREx0p6leORf-6dYb3H8hkqVqi2InhWPjHYFgy1DjveauhPCyyYoVlR2E41VbGH162IrfAI2VTjLB0g9u_ByCkhgBmsXbiNP56fC6kh5d_q3vAF3Bh7ygNY_gJTptKnJY24A5AOG6uXUWjzKdBiYNrgi7KHjM7eEEfUiXGt7bibs4w?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GzmT1owSpd12I7Ct-D0-ZfgXdbqoJ08Zfw8ue9DfMtKuS88Opaj-a52xa30Y_zESN1kBoBGXP3vDQpG2pfUJqHnsPm_URE7fzhr95pT55FzRE935oz5H3-GwFYzlSgqll7OwUvFg02fv9_eIOjNC7veBr8y3wf6BvTUqtOfKpFqkYRE588KSqeZsuYJRB3IZS8EiCFFHERMpw?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#poly-000000-10000-0</styleUrl>
