      <Placemark>
        <name>Muri Servii Tullii (Roma, Italia)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gzvh0PDSK9kJXGi14BZpvqSp7OY0G5r-pjkky0Dx9HrtC0nQHW_BjeMLOh89jV0Zq6iS_jJQa0wbDJe6wsQaTosl-PH-C4wIJK4M5weTA6qN-OPVnkaMzLXoQ0mbe5vYimO1Ch60PMtcGnnJ2Mt6_ZQN_HzOcOtHnXsyt0ac7yHPOVt5ehV2HdHB4Ub7_pQFPBhTP84AbrLeg?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Servian Walls, Rome.<br><br>The Servian Walls were a defensive barrier constructed around the city of Rome in the early 4th c. BC. <br><br>The wall was built of volcanic tuff and was up to 10 m (33 ft) in height in places, 3.6 m (12 ft) wide at its base, 11 km (6.8 mi) long, and is believed to have had 16 main gates, and it enclosed a total area of 608 acres. <br><br>In the 3rd c. AD it was superseded by the construction of the larger Aurelian Walls as the city of Rome grew beyond the boundary of the Servian Walls<br><br>The wall is named after the sixth Roman King, Servius Tullius.<br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_Gzkdi9_l84i8__zTK7mTE8eq7kivqBNpBdz-9CR59jzsN-1MvLZWw3dKH48w8eXOBk2I3fjdKZ9scDvkto3JN81k3uUOhyUUu1Qg9rHXjnwWOnI-qrPhgxfhyLF61qgjpb9P1JSNvGfTk6r14XZJPtJaE96mJFQE9kWgaTxcvrXHCYv-7jz2wL5cQkYpZMPpZbAvWat5y_1gA?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AE5a_GyvQoVjxvM06nEDWvZfetAdhKj_huHX0m0yrCr11j_Yco09g8_ksq2U6znY5ji7YgSuqyvlXrpbUq9RlGkbJCrEL_h47rLwo8cnXexUsGIn_nHQu9zUgj3We4yzmqHhH4Mj8tftfj8tjNRh1iGZ7lpEvgRdZobbrLy8FEGZs_zMvyAlY_bGUSYV8mER9jzohbh34CGoFHDjzg?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
